    "ls|LS17_S7_U_280": "GOVERNMENT \nOF \nINDIA\n \nMINISTRY \nOF \nMICRO,\n \nSMALL \nAND \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION No.\n \n*280\n \nTO BE \nANSWERED \nON\n \n16.12.2021\n \n \nMSME\ns\n \nIN WEST BENGAL\n \n \n*280.\n \n \nSHRI RAJU BISTA:\n \n \n \nWill \nthe \nMinister \nof \nMICRO, SMALL \nAND \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES \nbe pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(a)\n \nthe number of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) functioning in \nWest Bengal as on date;\n \n \n(b)\n \nthe data on the number of MSMEs in Darjeeling and Kalimpong districts;\n \n(c)\n \nthe details of loans sanctioned under the MUDRA Yojana in Darjeeling and \nKalimp\nong districts since the inception of the scheme; and \n \n(d)\n \nthe details of loans disbursed to the MSME sector under Prime Minister Aatma \nNirbhar Bharat Scheme and the number of MSMEs benefitted therefrom in Darjeeling \nand Kalimpong districts?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER\n \nOF \nMICRO, SMALL \nAND \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(\nSHRI\n \nNARAYAN RANE\n)\n \n \n(a) to (d): \n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION No. 280  FOR ANSWER ON 16.12.2021\n \n(a)& (b)\n:\n \nAs per Udyam Registration Portal, the total number of classified micro, \nsmall and medium enterprises registered in Darjeeling and Kalimpong districts and in \nthe state of West Bengal as on 12.12.2021 is given below:\n \nDistrict/State*\n \nMicro\n \nSmall\n \nMedium\n \nTotal\n \nDARJEELING\n \n5,258\n \n625\n \n54\n \n5,937\n \nKALIMPONG\n \n354\n \n12\n \n0\n \n366\n \nWEST BENGAL\n \n1,53,190\n \n13,430\n \n1,604\n \n168,224\n \n    \n*From 01.07.2020 to 12.12.2021\n \n \n(c)\n:\n \nThe details\n \nof loan sanctioned under Mudra Yojana in Darjeeling and \nKalimpong districts are given below:\n \n \nDistrict\n \nNumber of Accounts \nSanctioned\n \nSanctioned Amount\n \n(Rs in Crore)\n \nDARJEELING*\n \n8,57,840\n \n4,220.90\n \nKALIMPONG*\n \n8,377\n \n55.58\n \n*Mudra Portal (District wise data is available since 01.04.2016 till 26.11.2021)\n \n(d)\n:\n \nThe details of loan disbursed in Darjeeling and \nKalimpong districts under \nEmergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS) under Aatma Nirbhar Bharat \nScheme is given below:\n \n \nDistrict\n \nEmergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme\n \nNumber of \nDisbursement\n \nDisbursement \nAmount\n \n(Rs in Crore)\n \nDARJEELING\n \n67,564\n \n378.04\n \nKALIMPONG\n \n1,788\n \n5.38\n \n \nUnder C\nredit Guarantee Scheme for Subordinate Debt (CGSSD), the number\n \nof\n \nguarantees approved and amount of guarantees approved in West Bengal were 25 \nand Rs.2.06 crore respectively as on 03.12.2021.\n \n*\n**\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_281": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †281 \nANSWERED ON 30.11.2021 \n \nConstruction of Stadium to Promote Sports \n \n†281. SHRI DULAL CHAND GOSWAMI: \nSHRI CHANDESHWAR PRASAD: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to construct stadiums at \ndistrict/block/panchayat level in the States to promote sports in the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the details of the progress made in \nthis regard so far; and \n \n(c) the details of the number of stadiums constructed so far  at \nblock/panchayat level in the country during the last two years, State -wise \nincluding Katihar, Jehanabad, Gaya and Arwal district of the state of Bihar? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR } \n \n(a) to (c) ‘Sports’ being a State subject, the primary responsibility to \nconstruct stadiums  at district/block/panchayat level  rests with the \nState/Union Territory Governm ents. The Union Government s upplements \ntheir efforts. The stadiums in various parts of the country, including Bihar, \nare under the jurisdiction of respective bodies/departments of State/UT \nGovernments. As such, the information about them is not maintained in this \nMinistry. However, t his Ministry has sanctioned 267 sports infrastructure \nprojects of various categories across the country under the Khelo India \nScheme, which includes 11 projects in Bihar. \n \n**** ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_282": "1 \n \nO.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURAL RESEARCH & EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 282 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021 \n \nAGRICULTURAL TECHNIQUES \n \n282. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE    \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether any scheme is being run by the Government to provide information to \nthe farmers regarding latest agriculture techniques;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the total number of farmers benifitted under said scheme in the  State of Uttar \nPradesh, district-wise? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h    (SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) & (b) The Government has set up a network of Krishi Vigyan Kendras \n(KVKs) in the Country to provide information to the farmers about latest agriculture \ntechniques. The activities of KVKs in clude On -farm testing to identify the location \nspecificity of technology under various farming systems; Frontline demonstration to \nestablish the production potential of improved agricultural technologies on the \nfarmers; fields; Capacity development of fa rmers for knowledge and skill up \ngradation; providing farm advisories using ICT and other media means on varied \nsubjects of interest to famers; and production of quality seeds and planting materials \nfor availability to the farmers. In order to develop aware ness of improved agricultural \ntechnology among the farmers, KVKs take up a large number of extension activities. \n(c) District wise number of farmers benefitted under different activities of KVKs in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh during 2020-21 is given in Annexure-I. \n \n******* \n  \n\n2 \n \nANNEXURE-I \n [Part (c) of Lok Sabha USQ No.282 dated 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021] \n \nDistrict wise number of farmers benefitted under di