    "ls|LS17_S7_U_283": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.283 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 17TH DECEMBER, 2021 \n \n \nM.D. SEATS IN MEDICAL COLLEGES \n \n*283. DR. MAHESH SHARMA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the total number of seats for M.D. in Nephrology, Neurology, Cardiology and \nOncology available in various Medical colleges in the country, college -wise and \nState/UT-wise;  \n \n(b) the details indicating the number of M.Ds. passed out from medical colleges in the \ncountry during the last three years;  \n \n(c) whether the number of M.Ds. passing out every year from medical colleges is \nadequate to meet the requirements of the country;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(e) if not, the steps taken/proposed to be taken by the Government to enhance the seats \nin the above categories? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE  \n(DR. MANSUKH MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 283* FOR 17TH DECEMBER, 2021 \n \n(a) & (b) As informed by National Medical Commission, MD Courses are not available \nin Nephrology, Neurology and Cardiology. However, DM Courses are available in these \nspecialities. There are 396 seats of MD in Radiation Oncology in 87 Medical colleges. \nThe college-wise and State/UT wise details of seats are at Annexure.   \n(c) to (e) The Government has taken following steps to further increase the availability \nof medical seats/ doctors in the country: - \ni. Centrally Sponsored Scheme for strengthening/ upgradation  of existing State \nGovernment/Central Government Medical Colleges to increase MBBS and PG \nseats. \nii. Central Sector Scheme for upgradation of Government Medical Colleges by \nconstruction of Super Specialty Blocks. A total of 75 projects have been approved \nand 53 have been completed. \niii. Under Central Sector Scheme for setting up of new AIIMS, 22 AIIMS have been \napproved. Undergraduate courses have started in 18 AIIMS. \niv. DNB qualification has been recognized for appointment as faculty to take care of \nshortage of faculty.  \nv. DNB diploma courses have been approved in 8 broad specialities. \nvi. The ratio of teachers to students has been rationalized to increase the number of \npostgraduate medical seats in the country. \nvii. By amending the regulations, it has been made mandatory for all medical colleges \nto start PG courses within 3 years from the date of their MBBS recognition \n/continuation of recognition. \n  \n\nAnnexure \nState & College wise List of MD (Radio Therapy/ Radiation Oncology) Course \n \nS.No. State College Name No. of Seats \n1  \nAndhra Pradesh \nSri Venkateswara Institute of Medical Sciences \n(SVIMS) , Tirupati \n3 \nGuntur Medical College, Guntur 2 \nNRI Medical College, Guntur 3 \nGSL Medical College, Rajahmundry 2 \n2  \nAssam \nAssam Medial College, Dibrugarh  1 \nDr. B. Borooah Cancer Institute (Regional Cancer \nCentre), Guwahati \n5 \n \nBihar \nPatna Medical College, Patna  - \nIndira Gandhi Institute of Medical \nSciences,Sheikhpura, Patna \n4 \n3 \nChandigarh \nPostgraduate Institute of Medical Education & \nResearch, Chandigarh \n4 \nGovernment Medical College, Chandigarh 4 \n4 Chattisgarh Pt. J N M Medical College, Raipur  6 \n5 \nDelhi \nMaulana Azad Medical College, New Delhi  5 \nAll India Institute of Medical Sciences, New Delhi 12 \nVardhmanMahavir Medical College &Safdarjung \nHospital, Delhi \n6 \n6 Gujarat B J Medical College, Ahmedabad  9 \nMP Shah Medical College,Jamnagar  1 \n7 \nHaryana \nPt. B D Sharma Postgraduate Institute of Medical \nSciences, Rohtak (Haryana) \n6 \nMaharishi Markandeshwar Institute Of Medical \nSciences & Research, Mullana, Ambala \n2 \n8 Himachal \nPradesh \nIndira Gandhi Medical College, Shimla  4 \n9 J&K Sher-I-Kashmir Instt. Of Medical Sciences, Srinagar  5 \n10 \nKarnataka \nKasturba Medical College, Manipal 3 \nKidwai Memorial Institute of Oncology, Bangalore 9 \nM S Ramaiah Medical College, Bangalore 5 \nBangalore Medical College and Research Institute, \nBangalore \n3 \nSt. Johns Medical College, Bangalore 2 \nKasturba Medical College, Mangalore 2 \nA J Institute of Medical Sciences & Research Centre, \nMangalore \n3 \nFather Mullers Medical College, Mangalore 3 \nVydehi Institute Of Medical Sciences & Research \nCentre, Bangalore  \n8 \n11 \nKerala \nMedical College, Thiruvananthapuram 6 \nT D Medical College, Alleppey (Allappuzha) 3 \nAmala Institute of Medical Sciences, Thrissur 1 \nRegional Cancer Centre, Thiruvanthapuram 8 \nGovernment Medical College, Kozhikode, Calicut 4 \nAmrita School of Medicine, Elamkara, Kochi  3 \nGovernment Medical College, Thrissur 2 \n\nGovernment Medical College, Kottayam 2 \n12 \nMadhya \nPradesh \nM G M Medical College, Indore 4 \nGandhi Medical College, Bhopal 4 \nAll India Institute of Medical Sciences, Bhopal  3 \nNetajiSubhash Chandra Bose Medical College, \nJabalpur \n5 \nChirayu Medical College and Hospital, \nBairagarh,Bhopal \n2 \nSri Aurobindo Medical College and Post Graduate \nInstitute , Indore \n5 \n13 \nMaharashtra \nRural Medical College, Loni 5 \nTata Memorial centre, Mumbai 18 \nBhabha Atomic Research Centre,Mumbai - \nGovernment Medical College, Aurangabad 2 \nMahatma Gandhi Institute of Medical Sciences, \nSevagram, Wardha \n1 \nGovernment Medical College, Nagpur 2 \n14 Manipur Regional Institute of Medical Sciences, Imphal 4 \n15 Orissa SCB Medical College, Cuttack 6 \n16 \nPondicherry \nJawaharlal Institute of Postgraduate Medical Education \n& Research, Puducherry \n7 \nSri Venkateswaraa Medical College, Hospital & \nResearch Centre, Pondicherry \n2 \n17 Punjab Christian Medical College, Ludhiana 3 \nGuru Govind Singh Medical College, Faridkot 5 \n18 \nRajasthan \nDr SN Me