    "ls|LS17_S7_U_284": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF CHEMICALS AND PETROCHEMICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. *284 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.12.2021 \nSetting up of Plastic Parks \n***** \n \n*284: SHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a whether Plastic Parks are set up by the Government; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to set up a plastic park in Darbhanga \n district of Bihar for i nnovative management of plastic waste/recycling and for \n employment generation at the grassroot/local level; \n \n(d) if so, the time by which it is likely to be set up; and  \n \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \n(DR. MANSUKH MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.284 \nfor answer on 17.12.2021 regarding ' Setting up of Plastic Parks'. \n \n(a) & (b) Yes, Sir. T he Department of Chemicals & Petrochemicals implement s \nthe scheme for Setting up of Plastic Parks with an aim to develop an ecosystem with \nstate-of-the-art infrastructure building and enabling common facilities through cluster \ndevelopment approach, to cons olidate and synergize the capacities of the domestic \ndownstream plastic processing Industry. Under the scheme, Government of India \nprovides grant funding up to 50% of the project cost, subject to a ceiling of Rs. 40.00 \ncrore per project. The remaining project cost is to be funded by the State Government, \nbeneficiary industries and by loan from financial institutions. \n \nSo far, eight Plastic Parks have been approved and two are in the process of getting \nfinal approval . These Plastic parks are located in the States of Assam, Madhya \nPradesh (two Plastic Parks), Odisha, Jharkhand, Tamil Nadu, Uttarakhand and \nChhattisgarh currently in various stages of completion. The details of these Plastic \nParks are as under: \n \n1. Madhya Pradesh (Tamot):  The Pla stic Park at Tamot  has completed \nphysical infrastructure and one unit is functional in the Plastic Park. \n \n2. Madhya Pradesh (Bilaua): The Plastic Park at Bilaua is at various stages \nof implementation. \n \n3. Odisha (Paradeep) : The work related to development of physical \ninfrastructure is almost completed. \n \n4. Jharkhand (Deoghar) : The work related to development of physical \ninfrastructure is in progress. \n \n5. Tamil Nadu (Thiruvallur) :  The work related to development of physical \ninfrastructure is in progress. \n \n6. Assam (Tinsukia): The work related to development of physical \ninfrastructure is in progress. \n \n7. Uttarakhand (Sitarganj): The Plastic Park at Sitarganj was approved on \n3rd December, 2020 and currently the work related to development of \nphysical infrastructure is in progress. \n\n \n8. Chhattisgarh (Sarora): The Plastic Park in Raipur, Chhattisgarh has been \napproved recently on 13.04.2021 and the work is yet to start. \n \n9. Uttar Pradesh (Gorakhpur): In-principle approval accorded. \n \n10. Karnataka (Ganjimutt, Mangaluru): In-principle approval accorded. \n \n \n(c) to (e) No, Sir. Since, no application has been received from the State Government \nfor setting up a Plastic Park at Darbhanga, the Department could not take any action \nw.r.t. setting up a Plastic Park at Darbhanga, Bihar.    \n******* \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_285": "������������������� �\n������������������������������������ �\n����������������������������� �\n�\n���� ����� �\n�\n��������������������� ����� �\n������������������ ����� ��� �� �\n�\n������������ ��������������� �\n�\n��� ������ �������������� ��\n�\n��������������������������������������� ���������������������\n������ �\n�\n���� �������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������� �\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ��������� ��� ���������� ����� ������\n����������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�\n������ �\n������������� �\n������������������������ �\n�������� ������������������ ���\n�\n�������������������������������������������������������������������� ���\n��������������� ���������� �\n�\n����� � ������������ � ������� �\n� � ���������� � �������� ������ ���������� ����� ����� �������\n������ ���������� ��������������������� �\n� �\n������������������������������������������������������������������� ���\n�������������������� �\n�\n������",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_286": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AYUSH \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.286 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17TH DECEMBER, 2021 \n \n \nINFRASTRUCTURE DEVELOPMENT FOR AYUSH \n \n*286. SHRI A. GANESHAMURTHI:  \nSHRI DILESHWAR KAMAIT: \n \nWill the Minister of AYUSH be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the details of fund allocation for infrastructural development under National AYUSH \nMission (NAM) in the country, State/UT-wise including Tamil Nadu and Bihar;  \n \n(b) whether any special grant or aid has been provided for setting up of educatio nal \ninstitutions for AYUSH system of medicine/treatment in Tamil Nadu, Puducherry and \nBihar; and  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF AYUSH \n  \n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL) \n \n(a) to (c)   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.286* FOR 17TH DECEMBER, 2021 \n \n(a) The Government of India has launched Centrally Sponsored Scheme of National \nAYUSH Mission (NAM) implementing through States/UTs including Tamil Nadu and \nBihar. Under NAM financial assistance has been provided to the State/UT Governments \nincluding Tamil Nadu and Bihar for overall development of AYUSH system which also \nincludes infrastructural development. The allocation of funds under NAM is based on the \nproposals reflected in the State Annual Action Plans (SAAPs) and resource pool \ncommunicated to States/UTs as per the NAM guidelines. The details of fund approved for \ninfrastructural development under National AYUSH Mission is at Annexure. \n(b) & (c) Public health is a State subject. Setting up of educational institution for AYUSH \nsystem of medicine in Tami l Nadu, Puducherry and Bihar comes under purview of \nrespective State/UT Governments. However, under NAM, there is provision of \nestablishment of new AYUSH Colleges in the States where availability of AYUSH \nteaching institutions is inadequate in Government S ector. Under NAM, Ministry of Ayush \nhas not received proposal through State Annual Action Plan (SAAP) for establishment of \nnew AYUSH educational institution from State/UT Government of Tamil Nadu, \nPuducherry and Bihar. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n \nAnnexure \nState/UT wise details of grants approved for upgradation of AYUSH Hospitals and upgradation of \nAYUSH Dispensaries from 2014-15 to 2021-22 \nSI. \nNo. Name of State/UTs \nAYUSH Hospitals AYUSH Dispensaries \nNo. of \nHospitals \nAmount \napproved  \n(Rs. in lakhs) \nNo. of \nDispensaries \nAmount \napproved  \n(Rs. in lakhs) \n1.  Andaman & Nicobar Islands 1 75.00 0 0 \n2.  Andhra Pradesh 10 188.00 23 130.00 \n3.  Arunachal Pradesh 1 5.20 0 0 \n4.  Assam 0 0 0 0 \n5.  Bihar 0 0 10 100.00 \n6.  Chandigarh 0 0 29 196.93 \n7.  Chhattisgarh 18 244.50 257 3002.46 \n8.  Dadra & Nagar Haveli and \nDaman & Diu 3 6.24 1 8.00 \n9.  Delhi 4 9.00 0 0 \n10.  Goa 0 0 0 0 \n11.  Gujarat 4 250.00 20 400.00 \n12.  Haryana 2 78.50 1136 1404.90 \n13.  Himachal Pradesh 105 409.35 1334 602.90 \n14.  Jammu & Kashmir 2 50.00 35 350.00 \n15.  Jharkhand 0 0 0 0 \n16.  Karnataka 15 1125.00 0 0 \n17.  Kerala 74 2356.30 39 689.30 \n18.  Ladakh 0 0 0 0 \n19.  Lakshadweep 1 29.26 8 28.00 \n20.  Madhya Pradesh 32 845.00 140 2800.00 \n21.  Maharashtra 0 0 0 0 \n22.  Manipur 2 141.00 2 35.00 \n23.  Mizoram 0 0 0 0 \n24.  Meghalaya 0 0 3 120.00 \n25.  Nagaland 0 0 4 80.00 \n26.  Odisha 2 85.00 56 1120.00 \n27.  Puducherry 0 0 7 7.00 \n28.  Punjab 0 0 10 61.74 \n29.  Rajasthan 11 152.50 868 7252.69 \n30.  Sikkim 0 0 0 0 \n31.  Tamil Nadu 2 95.00 0 0 \n32.  Telangana 4 300.00 57 615.00 \n33.  Tripura 2 333.82 8 160.00 \n34.  Uttar Pradesh 12 900.00 572 11347.97 \n35.  Uttarakhand 0 0 0 0 \n36.  West Bengal 0 0 240 782.60 \nTotal 307 7678.67 4859 31294.49 \n \n \n\n \nState/UT wise details of grants approved for AYUSH Health and Wellness Centres from 2019-20 to \n2021-22 \nS. No. Name of State / UT 