    "ls|LS17_S7_U_328": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *328 \n \nANSWERED ON 21.12.2021 \n \nPromotion of Sports \n \n*328.     SHRI GIRISH CHANDRA: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) the details of the Centrally Sponsored Schemes being \nimplemented by the Government for the promotion of sports in the \ncountry;  \n(b) the funds allocated under these schemes during each of the \nlast three years and the current year, sports-wise; and \n(c) the details of the expenditure incurred on these schemes \nduring the said period, year-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR] \n \n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN  REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c ) OF THE  \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *328 FOR 21 /12/2021 \nREGARDING PROMOTION OF SPORTS  ASKED BY SHRI GIRISH \nCHANDRA. \n \n(a): Presently, no Centrally Sponsored Scheme is being implemented \nby the Department of Sports. However, the Department of Sports , \nthrough the following Central Sector Schemes,  supplements efforts of \nthe State/UT Governments for development and promotion of sports: (i)  \nKhelo India ; (ii) A ssistance to National Sports Federations ;  (iii)  \nSpecial Awards to Winners in International sports events and their \nCoaches; (iv) National Sports Awards, (v) Pension to Meritorious Sports \nPersons; (vi) Pandit Deendayal Upadhyay National Welfare Fund  for \nSportspersons; (vii) National Sports Development Fund; and (viii) \nSports training centres through Sports Authority of India (SAI). Details \nof these schemes are in the public domain on the websites of this \nMinistry and SAI.  \n \n(b) and (c) Details of funds allocated and expenditure incurred  under \nthe schemes mentioned in part (a) during each of the last three years \nand the current year are given at Annexure. The Department of Sports \ndoes not maintain sports-wise allocation of funds. \n \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b ) to (c) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *328 TO BE ANSWERED \nON 21.12.2021 REGARDING “PROMOTION OF SPORTS” ASKED BY SHRI GIRISH CHANDRA: \n \n \n \n \n \n(Rs. in crore)  \n2018-19  \n \n2019-20  \n \n2020-21 \n \n2021-22 \n(upto  08.12.2021) \nS.No.  Scheme  Allocation Actual Allocation Actual Allocation Actual Allocation Actual \n1.  Sports Authority of India  395.00  395.00  615.00  615.00 500.00 612.21 660.41 470.16 \n2.  Khelo India  500.09  342.24  578.00  575.52 328.77 338.06 657.71 375.44 \n3.  Assistance to National Sports \nFederation  245.13  243.63   \n300.85  \n300.85 132.00 128.62 280.00 85.47 \n4.  Special (Cash) Awards  31.00  30.94  62.00  61.54 16.00 15.99 38.00 33.11 \n5.  National Sports Awards  2.00  1.83  2.00  1.65 7.50 7.25 \n6.  Pension to Meritorious Sports persons  30.00  29.77  47.00  46.99 14.00 13.22 15.00 4.92 \n7.  \nPandit Deendayal Upadhyay National \nWelfare Fund for  \nSportspersons  \n1.80  1.00  \n2.00  1.00 2.00 2.00 2.00 0.00 \n8.  National Sports Development Fund  2.00  2.00  77.15  77.15 7.23 7.23 25.00 0.00 \n Total   1207.02 1046.41  1684.00  1679.7 1007.5 1124.58 1678.12 969.10 \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_329": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF IDNIA\n \nMINISTRY O1F AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *329\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 21\nst\n \nDECEMBER, 2021\n \n \nSUBSIDY FOR AGRICULTURAL EXPORTS\n \n \n*329. \n \nSHRIMATI VANGA GEETHA\n \nVISWANATH:\n \nSHRI KOTHA PRABHAKAR REDDY:\n \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government extends sops or\n \nconcessions under transport and \nmarketing scheme for\n \nagri exports, through mandis and at purchase centres;\n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details and the results thereof, Stat\ne\n-\nwise;\n \nand\n \n \n(c) \n \nif not, the time by which such a scheme is\n \nproposed to be announced for the \ncountry including\n \nAndhra Pradesh and Telangana?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n(\na) to (c)\n:\n \n \nA statement is laid on the table of the House.\n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRE\nD TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n329\n \nFOR ANSWER ON \n21\n.12\n.2021\n \nBY \nSHRIMATI VANGA \nGEETHA \nVISWANATH & \nSHRI KOTHA PRABHAKAR REDDY\n \nREGARDING \n“\nSUBSID\nY FOR AGRICULTURAL EXPORTS\n”\n.\n \n \n(a) \nto \n(\nc\n)\n:\n \n  \nAs per the information received from Ministry of Commerce & Industry, \nGovernment has brought out a Central Sector Scheme\n-\n \n“Transport and Marketing \nAssistance\n \n(TMA)\n \nfor Specified Agriculture Products”\n-\n \nfor providi\nng assistance for the \ninternational component of freight and marketing of agricultural produce, which is likely to \nmitigate disadvantage of higher cost of transportation of export of specified agriculture \nproducts due to trans\n-\nshipment and to promote brand\n \nrecognition for Indian agricultural \nproducts in the specified overseas markets. Initially the Scheme was available for exports \neffected from 1.03.2019 to 31.03.2020 and was later extended for the exports effected up \nto 31.03.2021.Further continuation of t\nhe Scheme, for the exports effected up to \n31.12.2023, has been approved with some modifications to the scheme.\n \n \n \n \nPromotion of \nagricultural exports is a continuous process\n. \nAgricultural and \nProcessed Food Products Export Development Authority (APEDA)\n \nprovi\ndes assistance to \nits registered exporters and other stakeholders under Market Development component of \nits scheme \"Agriculture & Processed Foods E\nxport Promotion Scheme” of APEDA\n. Under \nthe scheme component, assistance is \nalso \nprovided for participation i\nn buyer\n-\nseller \nmeets, trade delegations, international trade fairs/exhibitions etc. Assistance is also \nprovided for new product/ market development through conducting feasibility studies, trial \nshipments, and registration of brands abroad. \nUnder this compo\nnent, assistance \nupto \n50% of the total cost subject to a ceiling of Rs. 10 lakhs per study per beneficiary\n \nis \navailable\n.\n \nfurther, the a\nssistance will be upto 75% of the total cost subject to a ceiling of \nRs. 10 lakhs per study per beneficiary if conducted\n \nby\n \nTrade Associations/\n \nIndian \nmissions\n  \n \nabroad/ \n \nCentral / state Govt. agencies/ exporters\n \n \nbelonging to North \n-\n \nEastern \n \n\n \n \n \nStates, difficult\n \nareas namely\n \nHimalayan and land locked states, Island    Union \nTerritories, SC/ST \nand women beneficiaries\n. \nFor act\nivities initiated by APEDA the funding \nshall be 100%\n. \nAPEDA\n \n \nalso disseminates trade data and market intelligence to its \nregistered exporters. Steps have also be taken to develop packaging standards and \ntransport protocols for specific products/ markets.\n \n \n \n \nDepartment of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare is implementing Mission for \nIntegrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) under which financial assistance is \nprovided for various horticulture activities including \npost harvest management activities \nwherein su\nbsidy is provided for the purchase of \nRefrigerated Transport vehicles\n \nthrough \nState Governments. The component is demand/ entrepreneur\n-\ndriven from among \nentrepreneurs, private companies, cooperatives, farmers groups etc through commercial \nventures for whic\nh assistance at the rate of 35% of admissible project cost in general \nareas and 50% in hilly and scheduled area is available as credit linked back ended \nsubsidy.\n \n \n \n \nGovernment ha\nd\n \nalso \nintroduced Kisan Rail trains to enable speedy movement of \nperishables i\nncluding fruits, vegetables, meat, poultry, fishery and dairy products from \nproduction or surplus regions to consumption or deficient regions. \nKisan Rail enables \nfarmers to utilize the vast railway network to gain access to distant, bigger and more \nlucrati\nve markets. Since the launch of first Kisan Rail service on 7\nth\n \nAugust, 2020 and \nupto 28\nth\n \nNovember, 2021, Indian Railways have operated approximately 1,642 Kisan \nRail services. \nThe State wise breakup of Kisan Rail trains is at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n. \n \n \n \n \nFurther, Min\nistry of Food Processing Industries (MoFPI) has extended the 50% \nsubsidy for transportation of any fruits \n \nand \n  \nvegetables\n  \n \nthrough any type of train service \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \nprovided by Indian Railways under Operation Greens\n-\n \nTomato, Onion and Potato (TOP) \nto all no\ntified fruits & vegetables (TOTAL) during 2020\n-\n21. \n \n \n \nKrishi UDAN Scheme was launched in August 2020, on international and national \nroutes to assist farmers in transporting agricultural products so that it improves their value \nrealisation. The scope of the\n \nKrishi Udaan Scheme was expanded by including more \ndistricts/airports across the country with an aim to extend benefit to the farmers. The \nKrishi UDAN is ongoing Scheme and agriculture products have been transported from the \nvarious destinations in the co\nuntry.\n \nMinistry of Civil Aviation has extended the incentives \nto the freighters and passenger to cargo flights carrying Agri\n-\n \nproduce in the selected \nairports under Krishi UDAN 2.0.\n \nKrishi UDAN 2.0 primarily focuses on transporting \nperishable food products\n \nfrom the hilly are\nas, northeastern states and tribal areas. The \nscheme aims to ensure seamless, cost\n-\neffective, time\n-\nbound air transportation and \nassociated logistics for all Agri\n-\nproduce originating especially from Northeast, hilly and \ntribal regions of the country.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nState\n-\nwise break up of Kisan Rail trains\n \n \nSl.No\n \nState\n \nNo. of services\n \n1\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n126\n \n2\n \nAssam\n \n1\n \n3\n \nGujarat\n \n48\n \n4\n \nKarnataka \n \n45\n \n5\n \nMaharashtra\n \n1239\n \n6\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n56\n \n7\n \nPunjab\n \n2\n \n8\n \nTelangana\n \n48\n \n9\n \nTripura\n \n1\n \n10\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n36\n \n11\n \nWest Bengal\n \n40\n \n \n \nTotal \n \n1642\n \n \n*****\n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_330": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n MINISTRY OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. *330 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 21.12.2021) \nAKASHVANI KENDRAS   \n*330.   SHRIMATI JYOTSNA CHARANDAS MAHANT:   \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a)  the details of total number of Akashvani Kendras currently \noperational under Prasar Bharati across the country, State/UT -\nwise including the State of Chhattisgarh;  \n(b) the details of the number of the said centres which have become \npaperless and have adopted the ‘e-office’ system;  \n(c) whether the employees at the said centres have adapted \nthemselves to the ‘e -office’ system for the operation of the said \ncentres;  \n(d) whether any efforts are being made to make the remaining \ncentres paperless;  \n\n(e) if so, the details and the time by which the said centres are \nproposed to be made paperless, State/UT -wise including the \nState of Chhattisgarh; and  \n(f) the total number of Akashvani Kendras currently operational and \nalso the number of non -operational centres in the State of \nChhattisgarh? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING; AND \nMINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS  \n(SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR) \n(a) to (f) A statement is laid on the Table of House. \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f ) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *330 FOR ANSWER ON 21.12.2021. \n(a) AIR has 500 Akashvani broadcasting centre s currently operational \nacross the country. State/UT-wise numbers are given at Annexure. \n(b) to (e) Offices of Prasar Bharati  across th e country are using \ndifferent modules of e -office for paperless operation including offices \nin All India Radio. \nEmployee centric modules such as eLeave, eTour are used by the \nemployees across the network. The e -file module, which is mainly \nused for process ing administrative and other matters in various \noffices, has been adopted by most of the offices for paperless working.     \nThe usage of e -file module by different offices in All India Radio is \nregularly being monitored.  Online training sessions are condu cted \nregularly to increase its effective usage by all the concerned staff in \nthe country including the state of Chhattisgarh.    \n(f) There are 13 AIR broadcasting centres operational in the State of \nChhattisgarh and all are using e-Office. \n**** \n\nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE AS  REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *330 FOR ANSWER ON 21.12.2021 \nSTATE/UT-WISE NUMBERS OF AIR BROADCASTING STATIONS  \n \nS. No.    States \n \nTotal  AIR \nStations \n1.  Andhra Pradesh 14 \n2.  Arunachal Pradesh 39 \n3.  Assam 23 \n4.  Bihar 16 \n5.  Chhattisgarh 13 \n6.  Goa 1 \n7.  Gujarat 17 \n8.  Haryana 5 \n9.  Himachal Pradesh 16 \n10.  Jharkhand  14 \n11.  Karnataka 20 \n12.  Kerala 12 \n13.  Madhya Pradesh     25 \n14.  Maharashtra 30 \n15.  Manipur 9 \n16.  Meghalaya  7 \n17.  Mizoram 13 \n18.  Nagaland 10 \n19.  Odisha 21 \n20.  Punjab 8 \n21.  Rajasthan  26 \n22.  Sikkim   16 \n23.  Tamilnadu 15 \n24.  Telangana 11 \n25.  Tripura 18 \n26.  Uttar Pradesh  29 \n27.  Uttarakhand 22 \n28.  West Bengal  16 \nUnion Territory  \n29.  UT (A & N Island) 1 \n30.  UT(Delhi)  1 \n31.  UT (Chandigarh) 1 \n32.  UT (Dadra, Nagar Haveli, Daman & Diu) 3 \n33.  UT (Lakshadweep and Minicoy Islands) 1 \n34.  UT(Puducherry) 2 \n35.  UT (Jammu & Kashmir) 16 \n36.  UT (Ladakh) 9 \nTotal 500 \n\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_331": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.331 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 30.11.2021 \n  \nFunds allocated for TOP Scheme \n  \n331. SHRI ABDUL KHALEQUE: \n  \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the sports persons from North East excelling at \ninternational levels over the post few years, if so, the details thereof; \n  \n(b) whether funds allocated for the Target Olympic Podium (TOP) \nscheme is sufficient and if so, the details thereof along with the \nprogress of the scheme; \n  \n(c) if not, the manner in which the Government will generate fund for \nthe above mentioned scheme and overall sports development; \n  \n(d) whether Karate has been included in Olympics Game and if so, the \nother steps taken by the Government to develop Karate; and \n  \n(e) whether the Government would consider establishing a State-of-\nthe-art sports training facility in Barpeta Lok Sabha Constituency of \nAssam and if so, the details thereof? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER FOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR] \n  \n(a): Yes, Sir. Sports persons from North East are excelling at \ninternational levels over the past few years. The North-Eastern States \nin India are home to some of India’s most recognised international \n\nplayers such as, Ms. M.C. Mary Kom - 2012 Olympics bronze medallist \nand a five-time world amateur-boxing champion, footballer Baichung \nBhutia, boxer L. Sarita Devi, silver medallist at the 2014 Glasgow \nCommonwealth Games, Jayanta Talukdar, Gold Medallist and Arjuna \nAward winner, weightlifter K. Sanjita Chanu, who won gold at the 2014 \nGlasgow Commonwealth Games, etc. \n  \nIn Tokyo Olympics 2020, out of 7 medal winners, 2 medal winners are \nfrom North-East States i.e., Ms. Mirabai Chanu (Weightlifting) - Silver \nMedal and Ms. Lovlina Borgohain (Boxing) - Bronze Medal. \n  \nFurther, 18 medals were won by athletes from North-Eastern States in \nAsian Games 2018 and Commonwealth Games 2018. \n  \n(b) & (c):  Target Olympic Podium Scheme (TOPS) was formulated in \nJuly 2014 under the overall ambit of National Sports Development \nFund (NSDF) with the aim to identify, groom and prepare potential \nmedal prospects for Olympic and Paralympic Games. No separate \nfunds are allocated for the Scheme. Funds are being released from \nNSDF to Sports Authority of India (SAI) for this Scheme. The details of \nblock grant released from NSDF to SAI for Target Olympic Podium \nScheme (TOPS) are given below: \nYear Amount Received (in Crore Rupees) \n2016-17 20.00 \n2017-18 10.00 \n2018-19 10.00 \n2019-20 08.50 \n2020-21 05.00 \n\n2021-22 12.00 \nTOTAL 65.50  \n \nIn addition, Rs.25.06 crore has been released by NSDF to SAI from \n2017-18 to till date for Out of Pocket Allowance (OPA) under TOPS. \n  \n(d):   Karate is not included in Paris 2024 Olympic Games. \n  \n(e):  At present, there is no such proposal. \n  \n**** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_332": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 332 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 30.11.2021) \n \nCELEBRATION OF AZADI KA AMRIT MAHOTSAVA \n \n332. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) the details of programmes organized by the Government in pursuit of \ncelebration of Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsava; and \n(b) the details of the programmes proposed to be organized during the cours e of \ncelebration of Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav in the days ahead? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING; AND  \nMINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n[SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR] \n \n(a) & (b) Celebrations of Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav  commenced on \n12.03.2021 starting a 75 week countdown to 75 th anniversary of our country’s \nIndependence and will end post a year on 15 th August, 2023. It is an intensive, \ncountrywide campaign focusing on citizen participation as Jan Andolan with a \nwhole-of-Government approach with large number of events being organized by \nthe Central Government, State Governments, etc., in various parts of the \ncountry. The Ministry of Culture, which is the nodal ministry for celebrations of \nAzadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav, has info rmed that up to 24 th November, 2021, 6714 \nprogrammes have been organized by the various Ministries of the Government \nof India under the Mahotsav. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_333": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 333\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30\nth\n \nNOVEMBER, 2021\n \n \nAGRICULTURAL SYSTEMS\n \n \n333. \n \nSHRI S. JAGATHRAKSHAKAN:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the pandemic has exposed both the strengths and the vulnerabilities of \nIndia‘s agri food systems, and has also emphasized the need for agr\nicultural market \nreforms and digital solutions to connect farmers to markets, create safety nets, ensure \nreasonable working conditions, and decentralize the agri food systems to make them \nmore resilient; and\n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details of the steps taken by th\ne Government in this regard, and if not, \nthe reasons therefor?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n       \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH\n \nTOMAR)\n \n(a) & (b):\n \nAs per Provisional Estimates of Annual National Income, released \nby \nNational Statistical Office (NSO), Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation \n(MoSPI) on 31st, May 2021, the share of Agriculture and Allied Sectors in total Gross \nValue Added (GVA) of the country has increased from 18.4% in 2019\n-\n20 to 20.2% in\n \n2020\n-\n21 at current prices.\n \n       \nThe Gross Value Added of Agriculture and Allied Sectors at current price has \nincreased from 33.94 lakh crore in 2019\n-\n20 to 36.16 lakh crore in 2020\n-\n21.\n \n \n \n \n \nIn order to facilitate the marketing of agricultural produce of \nthe farmers during \nthe COVID\n-\n19 pandemic, the Government had issued advisory to States/Union \nTerritories (UTs) to facilitate Direct Marketing, enabling direct purchase from the \nfarmers/ Farmer Producer Organizations (FPOs)/ Cooperatives etc. by liberalizin\ng \nregulations under respective State Agricultural Produce Market Committee (APMC) \nActs.\n \n\n \nThe Government also issued advisories to States/UTs to ensure inter\n-\nstate and \nintra\n-\nstate movement of vehicles carrying the agriculture produce in addition to setting \nup of monitoring cell to keep watch and extend immediate help for seamless movement \nof such vehicles including coordination for issue of permits to trucks.\n \n \n \nFurther, in order to decongest wholesale markets, FPO trading module has been \nlaunched to facilita\nte FPOs to trade their agri produce from their collection centre \nwithout bringing the produce to APMC. Warehouse based trading module was also \nlaunched to enable farmers to sell their produce from WDRA registered warehouses \nnotified as deemed market\n \n \nFurth\ner, to address the transportation issues of Farmers and other stake holders \nduring Covid\n-\n19, the Government has launched the Kisan Rath Mobile App on \n17.04.2020.\n \n \nThe App facilitates the Farmers, FPOs and Traders to\n \npost their load \nrequests which are sent \nto transport aggregators and individual transporters who in turn \nrespond to the load requests.\n \n \nThe Government has taken necessary measures to ensure smooth sowing and \nharvesting operations during COVID\n-\n19 pandemic.\n \n \nAs per 3\nrd\n \nadvance estimates for \n2020\n-\n2\n1, total food grain production in the country is estimated at record 305.44 million \ntones which is higher by 7.94 million tonnes than the production of food grain during \n2019\n-\n20. Similarly, total horticulture production in 2020\n-\n21 is estimated to a record \n331.05 million tones which is an increase of about 10.6 million tone over that achieved \nin 2019\n-\n20.\n \n*****\n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_334": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 334 \nANSWERED ON-30.11.2021 \n  \nDEPARTMENTAL STANDING COMMITTEE AT VILLAGE/BLOCK LEVEL \n \n†334. SHRI SANJAY BHATIA: \n           \nWill the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government proposes to constitute the departmental Standing \nCommittee/Advisory Committee at the village level in all the panchayats of the country, \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to constitute the departme ntal Standing \nCommittee/Advisory Committee at block level across the country; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) whether the Government in coordination with the State Government of Haryana \nproposes to constitute the departmental Standing Committee/Advisory Committee, if \nso, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL) \n  \n(a) & (b) No, Sir. \n \n(c) Question does not arise. \n \n(d) No, Sir. \n \n*** \n ",
