    "ls|LS17_S7_U_351": "Page 1 of 3 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 351 \nANSWERED ON 30.11.2021 \n \nPromotion of Rural and Indigenous/Tribal Games \n \n351. SHRI JAYANT SINHA: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the games identified under the “promotion  of rural and indigenous/tribal \ngames” component of Khelo India; \n \n(b) the details and the number of annual national \ncompetitions/activities/demonstrations held for rural and indigenous/tribal \ngames since 2018 and the games for which competitions have been held; \n \n(c)  the  number  of  NGOs  and  sports  federations/ associations  to  whom  \nfinancial  support  has  been provided for promotion of these games since \n2018 and the amount given, State-wise; and \n \n(d) the number of top sports persons identified for these games, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR } \n \n(a) Mallakhamb, Kalaripayattu, Gatka, Thang -Ta, Yogasana and Silambam \nhave been identified for promotion by this Ministry  under the “Promotion of \nrural and indigenous/tribal games” component of the Khelo India Scheme. \n \n(b) Demonstration event s for Mallakhamb, Thang -Ta, Kalaripayattu and \nGatka were held during the 3rd edition of the Khelo India Youth Games, 2020 \nat Guw ahati, Assam. Further, thirty-six sports competitions/events were \norganised in 2019 -20 by this Ministry as a part of the  Ek Bharat S hreshtha \nBharat programme to promote indigenous and tribal games in various \ndisciplines, namely, Gatka, Roll Ball, Tug of War, Kalaripayattu, Thang -Ta, \nKho-Kho, Mallakhamb, Shooting Ball, Sqay, Kabaddi, etc. in different parts \nof the country. \n \n\nPage 2 of 3 \n \n(c) Four Nationa l Sports Federations (NSFs) have been provided financial \nassistance under  the “Promo tion o f rural and indigenous/tribal games” \ncomponent of the Khelo India Scheme  as per the d etails tabulated below. \nState-wise data is not maintained in this regard in this Ministry. \n \nS. No. Name of the Federation (NSF) Funds Released (in ₹ crore) \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \n(up to \n30.09.2021) \n1 Mallakhamb Federation of India - 2.34 1.47 0.06 \n2 Indian Kalaripayyattu \nAssociation \n- 0.61 0.21 0.50 \n3 National Gatka Association - 0.27 0.23 0.18 \n4 Thang-Ta Federation of India - 0.48 0.30 0.15  \nTotal - 3.70 2.20 0.89 \n \n(d) A to tal of 283 athletes have been identified in the disciplines of \nMallakhamb, Thang -Ta, Kalaripayattu and Gatka  who are being provided \nOut-of-Pocket Allowance (OPA) under the “Promotion of rural and \nindigenous/tribal games” component of the Khelo India Scheme . State-wise \ndetails of the same are at Annexure. \n\nPage 3 of 3 \n \nANNEXURE RE FERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 351 ANSWERED ON 30.11.2021 REGARDING \n“PROMOTION OF RURAL AND INDIGENOUS/TRIBAL G AMES” ASKED BY \nSHRI JAYANT SINHA, HON’BLE MEMBER OF LOK SABHA \n \nState-wise details of athletes being provided OPA under the “Promotion of \nrural and indigenous/tribal games” component of the Khelo India Scheme \n \nS. \nNo. \nState/UT No. of Athletes \nMallakhamb Kalaripayattu Thang-ta Gatka Total \n1 Andhra Pradesh 0 0 1 0 1 \n2 Assam 0 2 1 0 3 \n3 Chandigarh 0 0 0 7 7 \n4 Chhattisgarh 7 0 0 4 11 \n5 Delhi 0 3 8 4 15 \n6 Goa 1 0 0 0 1 \n7 Gujarat 2 0 1 0 3 \n8 Haryana 0 0 0 3 3 \n9 Jammu & Kashmir 0 1 0 0 1 \n10 Karnataka 2 7 0 0 9 \n11 Kerala 0 56 0 0 56 \n12 Madhya Pradesh 31 0 0 1 32 \n13 Maharashtra 34 1 5 2 42 \n14 Manipur 0 0 31 0 31 \n15 Puducherry 1 3 0 0 4 \n16 Punjab 0 0 0 29 29 \n17 Rajasthan 0 0 0 2 2 \n18 Tamil Nadu 24 5 0 0 29 \n19 Telangana 1 0 0 0 1 \n20 Uttar Pradesh 1 1 0 1 3 \nTotal 104 79 47 53 283 \n \n \n**** ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_352": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 352 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021/ AGRAHAYANA 9, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nTHREAT TO NATIONAL SECURITY \n \n352.   SHRI RITESH PANDEY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether there is any guideline for determining the threat to national security; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the basis and  criteria used to determine that a \nperson, institution, or a group of persons are a threat to national security; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons, therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n(a) to  (c): Security threat assessment is a continuous process. Based on \ninputs received from various agencies, threat assessment is done and \nappropriate security measures are taken, including appropriate pre -emptive \nand preventive action against individual (s) and institutions. Several \nmeasures have been taken by the Government to strengthen the security \narchitecture, such as strengthening the legal framework by amending the \nUnlawful Activities (Prevention) Act 1967, the National Investigation Agency \nAct 2008, A rms Act 1959, Modernization of Police and the Central Police \nArmed Forces (CAPFs), strengthening of border security grid and coastal \nsecurity, strengthening of the Multi -Agency Centre (MAC) and exchange of \ninformation and intelligence in various bilateral fora.  \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_353": " \n1 \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURAL RESEARCH & EDUCATION \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 353 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021 \n \n \nAGRICULTURAL UNIVERSITIES   \n \n \n353. SHRI BHAGWANT MANN:  \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE    \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h  be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has allocated funds to encourage education in \nagricultural universities located in Punjab to further boost the agriculture sector;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government is contemplating setting up a new agricultural university \nin Punjab to give a further boost to agricultural education; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nd`f\"k vkSj fdlku dY;k.k ea=h     (SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n(a)  Yes, Sir. \n(b) Financial support of Rs. 110.30 crore has been provided by the Indian Council \nof Agricultural Research (ICAR) to the Punjab Agricultural University (PAU), Ludhiana \nand Guru Angad Dev Veterinary and Animal Sciences University (GADVASU), \nLudhiana, Punjab during the period from 2017 -18 till date  for strengthening and \ndevelopment of the Universities. The details are at Annexures I. \n(c)   There is no such proposal for setting up of a new agricultural university in \nPunjab by the Government. \n(d) In view of reply to part (c), the question does not arise. \n******* \n \n \n\n \n2 \n \n \n \n \nAnnexure-I \n[Part (b) of Lok Sabha USQ No.353 dated 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021] \n \nSupport provided for strengthening and development of the Agricultural \nUniversities located in Punjab under the scheme “Strengthening and Development of \nHigher Agricultural Education in India” is as under: \n(Rs. in crore) \nS. No. Name of \nthe \nUniversities \n2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22  \n(till date) \nNAHEP Total \n1 \nGADVASU, \nLudhiana \n \n5.94 5.95 7.28 3.69 1.10 25.00 48.96 \n2 \nPAU, \nLudhiana \n \n10.77 7.12 12.36 9.49 1.60 20.00 61.34 \nTotal 16.71 13.07 19.64 13.18 2.70 45.00 110.30 \n  ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_355": " \n \n O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 355 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nGARIB KALYAN ROJGAR ABHIYAAN \n \n355.  SHRI SATYADEV PACHAURI: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has launched a  comprehensive employment-cum-rural pulic \nworks campaign named ‘Garib Kalyan Rojgar Abhiyaan (GKRA)’  to empower and \nprovide livelihood opportunities in areas/villages witnessing large number of returnee \nmigrant workers affected by devastating COVID-19; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the number  of beneficiaries, mandays employment \ngenerated and the expenditure incurred under the said scheme till date, State-wise; \n(c)  whether the said scheme has been successful; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof along with the steps  being taken to ensure effective and \ntimely implementation of the said scheme? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a) to (d)       The Garib Kalyan Rojgar  Abhiyaan (GKRA) was launched on 20 th June 2020 \nfor a period of 125 days with resource envelop of Rs.50,000 Crore to boost employment and \nlivelihood opportunities for migrant workers returning to villages and similar ly affected \ncitizens in rural area. The Abhiyaan adopted a multipronged strategy of providing immediate \nemployment & livelihood opportunities to the distressed, to saturate the villages with public \ninfrastructure and creation of livelihood assets to boost the income generation activities and \nenhance long term livelihood opportunities by giving focus on 25 works in 116 selected \ndistricts across 6 States namely Bihar, Jharkhand, Madhya Pradesh, Odisha, Rajasthan and \nUttar Pradesh. The Abhiyaan achieved employ ment generation of 50.78 Crore Persondays \nwith a total expenditure incurred of Rs. 39,293 Crore. State -wise detail of employment \ngenerated & expenditure incurred is given at Annexure. \n  \nA Committee of Secretaries (CoS) under the Chairpersonship of Cabinet Secretary was set up \nfor review of the Abhiyaan. There was a Central Coordinator for the Abhiyaan to coordinate \nwith the participating Departments/Ministries of the Central Government and with the Nodal \nOfficers of the State Governments. A district wise de dicated Central Nodal Officer (CNO) \nwas responsible for monitoring and facilitation of ground level implementation. At State \nLevel, each State under the Abhiyaan had appointed the Additional Chief Secretary/Principal \nSecretary/Secretary, In -charge of State  Rural Development Department as the State Nodal \nOfficer (SNO) for the Abhiyaan, who was responsible for implementation, monitoring and \noverall outcome of the Abhiyaan within the State. At district Level, a committee of all \nstakeholders was formed under th e Chairpersonship of District Collector/ District Magistrate \n/Deputy Commissioner of the Abhiyaan District for the implementation and monitoring. \n*****  \n\n \n \nAnnexure \n \nAnnexure referred in reply to parts (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.355 \ndue for answer on 30.11.2021 \n  \n  \nState-wise employment generated (in person-days) and total Expenditure \nS. No. State Employment Provided \n(In Persondays) \nTotal Expenditure \n(Rs. In Crore) \n1 Bihar 11,19,48,805 10,992 \n2 Jharkhand 1,32,51,929 1,396 \n3 Madhya Pradesh 9,99,01,931 6,819 \n4 Odisha 2,30,31,641 2,042 \n5 Rajasthan 15,39,17,007 8,715 \n6 Uttar Pradesh 10,58,17,358 9,330 \n  Total 50,78,68,671 39,293 \n  \n  \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_356": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUN\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n356\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n30\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, 2021\n \n \nPAYMENT OF INSURANCE CLAIMS UNDER PMFBY\n \n \n356\n. \nSHRI \nRAMESH CHANDRA MAJHI  :\n \n        \nSHRI ACHYUTANANDA SAMANTA :\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) whether insurance claims are being paid to farmers on time after crop damage/failure \nu\nnder the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY), if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether in many States, including Odisha, the payment of insurance claims for crop \nfailure in 2018\n-\n19, 2019\n-\n20 and 2020\n-\n21 is still pending, if so the details thereof; \n \n(c)\n \nwhether the Government proposes to take steps for payment of all these outstanding \nclaims; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the time by which the outstanding claims will be fully paid \nand if not, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) the\n \nsteps being taken by the Government to ensure that farmers are being \ncompensated properly especially during crop loss in cases of drought or deficient \nrainfall?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n(SHRI \nNARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to (e) : \nThe admissible claims under the \nPradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana \n(PMFBY)\n \nare generally paid by the \nconcerned \ninsurance companies within two months \nof completion of Crop Cutting Experiments (CCEs)/harvesting period and one month of \nnotification for invoking the risks/perils of prevented sowing, mid\n-\nseason adversity and \npost harvest losses subject to receipt of tot\nal share of premium subsidy from concerned \nGovernment within time. However, settlement of \nfew \nclaims in some States \nincluding \nOdisha \ng\not\n \ndelayed due to reasons like delayed transmission of yield data; late release \nof their share in premium subsidy, yield r\nelated disputes between insurance companies \nand States, non\n-\nreceipt of account details of some farmers for transfer of claims to the \nbank account of eligible farmers and National Electronic Fund Transfer (NEFT) related \nissues, erroneous/incomplete entry of\n \nindividual farmers data on National Crop \nInsurance Portal (NCIP), delay in remittance of farmers share of premium/non\n-\nremittance of farmers share of premium to concerned insurance company etc.   \n \n \n \n\n \nThis Department is regularly monitoring the implementati\non of PMFBY including \ntimely settlement of claims through weekly video conference of stakeholders, one to one \nmeetings with insurance companies/States etc.  Further, penalty provisions for late \nsettlement of claims by insurance companies and late release o\nf funds by State \nGovernments have also been stipulated under the revised/revamped operational \nguidelines of the scheme.  Insurance companies have to pay penal interest @12% per \nannum to the farmers for the period beyond the stipulated period in the PMFBY \nG\nuidelines from the date of receipt of final yield data from the State Government and \ncompletion of crop damage survey.\n \n \nFurther, this Department is regularly reviewing the schemes in consultation with \nState Governments and other stakeholders to streamline \nthe process for early \nsettlement of claims and to provide timely and adequate benefits to the eligible farmers \nunder the scheme.\n \n \nState\n-\nwise details of pending claims including Odisha, for the years 2018\n-\n19, \n2019\n-\n20 and 2020\n-\n21 are \nannexed\n. \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n \nState\n-\nWise Status of  Pending Claims under PMFBY for 2018\n-\n19, 2019\n-\n20 and 2020\n-\n21 as on \n25.11.2021\n \n(Rs. in crore)\n \nState/UT Name\n \nStates/UTs\n \nReported \nClaims\n \nPaid \nClaims\n \nClaims \nPending\n \nReason for \nPendency\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \nA & N Islands\n \n0.09\n \n0.01\n \n0.08\n \nPayment \nFailure\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n1,890.05\n \n1,885.76\n \n4.29\n \nPayment Failure\n \nGujarat\n \n2,778.08\n \n2,777.89\n \n0.18\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nHaryana\n \n948.01\n \n947.75\n \n0.27\n \nPayment Failure\n \nJharkhand\n \n684.94\n \n50.98\n \n633.95\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nKarnataka\n \n2,948.56\n \n2,947.99\n \n0.57\n \nPayment Failure\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n3,777.31\n \n3,777.14\n \n0.17\n \nPayment Failure\n \nMaharashtra\n \n6,149.46\n \n6,146.19\n \n3.27\n \nPayment Failure\n \nTelangana\n \n587.35\n \n148.92\n \n438.43\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nWest Bengal\n \n535.52\n \n529.85\n \n5.67\n \nPayment \nFailure; State \nSubsidy \nPending\n \n2018\n-\n19 Total\n \n \n29,341.04\n \n28,254.15\n \n1,086.89\n \n \n2019\n-\n20\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n1,259.01\n \n1,254.03\n \n4.98\n \nPayment Failure\n \nAssam\n \n21.27\n \n-\n \n21.27\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n1,314.60\n \n1,296.59\n \n18.02\n \nPayment Failure\n \nGujarat\n \n369.40\n \n111.67\n \n257.73\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nHaryana\n \n933.08\n \n928.36\n \n4.72\n \nPayment Failure\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n67.54\n \n66.61\n \n0.93\n \nPayment Failure\n \nJharkhand\n \n25.46\n \n-\n \n25.46\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nKarnataka\n \n1,572.28\n \n1,349.26\n \n223.02\n \nPayment \nFailure; Pending \nclarifications \nfrom State \nGovernment\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n5,991.92\n \n5,947.35\n \n44.57\n \nUnder Process\n \nMaharashtra\n \n6,757.36\n \n6,748.51\n \n8.85\n \nPayment Failure\n \nOdisha\n \n1,170.11\n \n1,152.81\n \n17.30\n \nPending \nclarifications \nfrom State \nGovernment\n \nPuducherry\n \n7.16\n \n6.23\n \n0.93\n \nPayment Failure\n \nRajasthan\n \n4,921.91\n \n4,920.18\n \n1.73\n \nPayment Failure\n \nTamil Nadu\n \n1,168.60\n \n1,136.46\n \n32.14\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nTelangana\n \n512.78\n \n-\n \n512.78\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n1,110.56\n \n1,086.56\n \n24.01\n \nPayment \nFailure; Pending \nclarifications \nfrom State \nGovernment\n \n2019\n-\n20 Total\n \n \n27,394.34\n \n26,195.86\n \n1,198.48\n \n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n(Provisional)\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n882.09\n \n853.95\n \n28.14\n \nState Subsidy \nPending; \n\nPayment Failure\n \nHaryana\n \n1,126.01\n \n1,118.64\n \n7.36\n \nState Subsidy \nPending; \nPayment Failure\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n36.22\n \n19.16\n \n17.06\n \nState Subsidy \nPending; \nPayment Failure\n \nKarnataka\n \n539.67\n \n485.80\n \n53.87\n \nUnder Process\n \nKerala\n \n103.03\n \n70.02\n \n33.01\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nMaharashtra\n \n1,311.35\n \n940.62\n \n370.73\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nOdisha\n \n550.24\n \n546.00\n \n4.25\n \nUnder Process\n \nPuducherry\n \n16.25\n \n-\n \n16.25\n \nState \nSubsidy \nPending\n \nRajasthan\n \n3,610.07\n \n3,449.35\n \n160.73\n \nState Subsidy \nPending; \nPayment Failure\n \nTamil Nadu\n \n952.44\n \n565.69\n \n386.75\n \nUnder Process; \nPayment Failure\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n491.12\n \n486.75\n \n4.36\n \nState Subsidy \nPending\n \nUttarakhand\n \n104.55\n \n99.72\n \n4.84\n \nPayment \nFailure\n \n2020\n-\n21 Total \n(Provisional)\n \n \n9,725.24\n \n8,637.89\n \n1,087.35\n \n \nGrand Total\n \n \n66,460.62\n \n63,087.90\n \n3,372.72\n \n \n* Cases where claims are settled have not been reported but are included in year totals\n \nNote :\n \nAll admissible claims are being transferred electronically to the bank account of the \neligible insured farmers directly or Aadhar Enabled Payment System (AEPS).  However, payment \nfailure occur due to error in banking details essential for money transfer s\nuch as \nmismatch in\n \nname in bank accounts, IFSC Code, Account number, dormant bank account and death of \neligible insured farmer without nomination etc., in transfer of claims amount.     \n \n \n*****\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_357": "O.I.H.\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUN\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n357\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n30\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, 2021\n \n \nNON\n-\nPAYMENT OF CROP INSURANCE COMPENSATION\n \n \n357. SHRI \nPRATAPRAO PATIL CHIKHLIKAR:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) whether\n \nthe Government is aware that the installment of crop insurance \ncompensation for the year 2020\n-\n21 has not been paid to the farmers in Nanded till date; \n \n(b) if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) whether the officials working in the concerned department are not\n \nserious in this \nregard; and \n \n(d) the time by which the insured compensation amount is likely to be paid to the \nfarmers?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (d) :   As reported by the State Government of Maharashtra total claims of Rs. \n223.35 crore  in Maharashtra including Rs. 7.40 crore for Nanded district for Kharif 2020 \nare pending for settlement by concerned insurance companies under Pradhan Mantri\n \nFasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY). Similarly claims of Rs. 48.36 crore including Rs. 17.98 \ncrore are pending for settlement for Rabi 2020\n-\n21 season.  These claims are pending \nas the State Government has not released its share of premium subsidy of Rs. 942.62 \ncror\ne for Kharif 2020 and Rs. 293.59 crore for Rabi 2020\n-\n21. \n \n \nThe PMFBY is a multi\n-\nagency scheme involving farmers, insurance companies, \nfinancial institutions and Governments both Centre and State, therefore \nthis \nDepartment \nis regularly monitoring the implem\nentation of PMFBY including timely settlement of \nclaims through weekly video conference of stakeholders, one to one meetings with \ninsurance companies/States etc.  Further, penalty provisions for late settlement of \nclaims by insurance companies and late rel\nease of funds by State Governments have \nalso been stipulated under the revised/revamped operational guidelines of the scheme.  \nInsurance companies have to pay penal interest @12% per annum to the farmers for \nthe period beyond the stipulated period in the P\nMFBY Guidelines from the date of \nreceipt of final yield data from the State Government and completion of crop damage \nsurvey.\n  \n \n*****\n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_358": "O.I.H.  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 358 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nDEEN DAYAL UPADHYAY GRAMEEN KAUSHAL YOJANA \n \n358.  SHRI SUKHBIR SINGH JAUNAPURIA: \nSHRI JAYANT SINHA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details and salient features of Deen Dayal  Upadhyay Grameen Kaushal Yojana \n(DDU-GKY) to  promote rural employment through skill development  including the \ndetails of the budgetary allocati on made during each of the last three years and the \ncurrent year along with the progress of the scheme, State/UT-wise; \n(b)  the number of training centres in Jharkhand and  the number of people trained, \nassessed, certified and placed through these centres, district-wise; \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to lift the cap  of 25 per cent on the permissible \nlimit of expenditure  under the DDU -GKY, if so, the details thereof and the  reasons \ntherefor; \n(d)  the number of rural youth benefitted through  this scheme  since its inception, \nState/UT-wise; \n(e)  whether all the villages have been covered in  this scheme, if so, the details thereof  \nincluding the reasons therefor, State/UT-wise; and \n(f)  whether any plan has been devised for the  revival of Rural Skill Develo pment \nProgramme by including more rural youth under the scheme to give  fillip to Make in \nIndia programme? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a) (i)    Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY) is a placement \nlinked skill development program for rural poor youth under NRLM. It has its origin in the \nwage employment linked “Special Projects” for skilling comp onent of the Swarnajayanti \nGram Swarojgar Yojana (SGSY), which was subsequently renamed as Aajeevika Skills when \nSGSY was converted as NRLM. Taking into account the focus on improving quality and \nemployment outcomes in the National Policy on Skill Development, and need to increase the \ncoverage of Skill Development programme in remote r ural areas, the scheme has been \nannounced as DDU -GKY on 25 th September 2014. The skilling program for rural youth has \nnow been refocused and re-priotorized to build the capacity of rural poor youth to address the \nneeds of domestic and global skill requirements. \n ii.      Salient features of DDU-GKY are as follows: \n Market-led, placement-linked training programme for rural youth undertaken in a PPP \nmode. \n\n \n Mandatory assured placement to 70% of the trained candidates. \n Focus on rural youth from poor families in the age group of 15 to 35 years. \n Social inclusion of candidates through mandatory coverage of socially  disadvantaged \ngroups, i.e for SC/ST-50%, Minorities- 15%, and Women 33%) \n Minimum Salary of Rs.6000 per month (after a three month training course). \n Post-placement support to candidates. \n Career progression support to training partners. \n In allocation of skills projects, primacy given to Training Partners who can  train and \nsupport overseas placement and captive placements. \n  \nDetails of the release made during each of the last three years and the current year along with \nthe progress of the scheme, State/UT-wise is given at Annexure-I (Table A&B). \n  \n(b). There are 37 operational Training Centres in Jharkhand, district –wise numb er of   \ntraining centres is given at Annexure-II.  \n  \n(c) DDUGKY is a demand driven programme within the overall allocation of National   Rural \nLivelihood Mission. Since 2015 there is no cap of 25% on the permissible limit of \nexpenditure under DDUGKY. \n \n(d) The number of rural youth benefitted through DDUGKY since its inception, State -wise is \ngiven at Annexure-III \n \n(e) DDUGKY programme covers rural poor youth in the age group of 15 -35 years with focus \non rural youth from poor families belonging to: a) MGNREGA w orker household if any \nperson from the household has completed 15 days of work, b) RSBY household, c) \nAntyodaya Anna Yojana card household, d) BPL PDS card households, e) NRLM -SHG \nhousehold, f) Participatory process of Identification of poor, g) Households  covered under \nauto inclusion parameters of SECC 2011. \nDetails : NA \n  \n(f) Skill training for the rural youth is being driven through the approved action plans under \nDDUGKY & RSETI. The target assigned in the Action Plan details are as under: \n  \nAction Plan Target \nSl. No Scheme Action Plan Target \n1 DDUGKY (2019-23) 1845977 \n2 RSETI (2021-22) 390265 \n  \n  \n   \n****** \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF  PART (A) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO 358 IN LOK SABHA ON 30.11.2021. \n  \nTable (A) 3 yrs and current yr Funds release status of DDU -GKY to State Govt.  (as on \n31.10.2021) \n                                                                                                                        (Rs. in lakhs) \nS.N. States 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \n1 A&N Islands    3.00 798.000   \n2 Andhra Pradesh 7247.000 7910.927     \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 113.500   1333.500   \n4 Assam 5128.600 10433.000 1328.400  156.890 \n5 Bihar 18294.000       \n6 Chhattisgarh   13913.066 60.000   \n7 Goa         \n8 Gujarat   8205.600     \n9 Haryana 5662.000 308.460 1318.000   \n10 Himachal Pradesh 183.600 2583.900 69.300   \n11 Jammu & Kashmir 12933.600 23376.590   117.472 \n12 Jharkhand 1160.000   4171.267   \n13 Karnataka         \n14 Kerala 9842.500   16381.561   \n15 Madhya Pradesh 3799.752 11558.000 319.325   \n16 Maharashtra 5327.000 21925.000     \n17 Manipur 2240.000 4468.791     \n18 Meghalaya 1884.000 2161.350 143.900 70.300 \n19 Mizoram 1431.588 237.000 552.500   \n20 Nagaland 2238.000 285.346 3727.800   \n21 Odisha 13889.600 16616.312 4135.000   \n22 Pudducherry   922.200 14.000   \n23 Punjab 1082.000 8073.500     \n24 Rajasthan 3282.000 