    "ls|LS17_S7_U_401": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 401 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nWORKS UNDERTAKEN UNDER MGNREGS IN KERALA \n \n401.  SHRI M.K. RAGHAVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether there has been any delay in payment of  Mahatma Gandhi National Rural \nEmployment Generation Scheme (MGNREGS) funds to States by the Central \nGovernment; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)  if not, the details of total amount of funds  allocated to the State of Kerala for the \nfinancial year 2021-22 under MGNREGS; and \n(d)  whether the Government maintains list of works undertaken under MGNREGS by the \nState and if so, the  list of works being undertaken by Kerala State in fi nancial year \n2021-22 and total amount of money spent under  MGNREGS by the State of Kerala \nfor FY 2021-22? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a) & (b)      Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment G uarantee Scheme (Mahatma \nGandhi NREGS) is a demand driven wage employment programme and funds are released to \nthe States/UTs on the basis of \"agreed to\" Labour Budget and performance of the States \nduring the financial year. \nFurther, the funds release under  Mahatma Gandhi NREGS is based on the provision of the \nAct and guidelines. As per guidelines, the first installment of the first tranche will be released \nin the first half of April after adjusting unspent balance available with the States and \nconsidering t he pending liabilities, if any. The 2nd Tranche is released on submission of \nproposal in the prescribed format by the State and subject to fulfillment of all the prescribed \nconditions. The funds for 2nd tranche can only be released after receipt of Audited  UC and \nAudited report of previous financial year \n  \nState/UT wise details of pending liabilities for wage component as on 25.11.2021 is given at \nAnnexure-I. \nState/UT wise details of pending liabilities for material component as on 25.11.2021 is given \nat Annexure-II.  \n  \n(c)   Under Mahatma Gandhi NREGS, no State/UT -wise (including State of Kerala) fund \nallocation is made, as it is a demand driven scheme. In the current financial year (FY) 2021 -\n22 (as on 25.11.2021), an amount of Rs. 2055.91 crore has been re leased to the State of \nKerala. \n  \n(d)   The details of category wise completed and ongoing works along with expenditure under \nMahatma Gandhi NREGS in the State of Kerala in the FY 2021-22 is given at Annexure-III. \n \n*****  \n\nAnnexure-I \n \nAnnexure-I referred in reply to part (a) & (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.401 \ndue for answer on 30.11.2021 \n  \nState/UT wise details of pending liabilities for wage component as on \n25.11.2021 \nSl. No. State/UT Wage Liability (Rs. in Lakh) \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 36990.81 \n2 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 6759.12 \n3 ASSAM 0.00 \n4 BIHAR 29618.61 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 2195.34 \n6 GOA 0.00 \n7 GUJARAT 0.00 \n8 HARYANA 1500.34 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 15670.17 \n10 JAMMU AND KASHMIR 10934.93 \n11 JHARKHAND 20693.82 \n12 KARNATAKA 50888.40 \n13 KERALA 0.00 \n14 LADAKH 54.23 \n15 MADHYA PRADESH 38258.58 \n16 MAHARASHTRA 10689.04 \n17 MANIPUR 0.00 \n18 MEGHALAYA 3395.59 \n19 MIZORAM 6923.41 \n20 NAGALAND 2277.99 \n21 ODISHA 0.00 \n22 PUNJAB 11112.44 \n23 RAJASTHAN 5765.71 \n24 SIKKIM 0.00 \n25 TAMIL NADU 13330.71 \n26 TELANGANA 4798.77 \n27 TRIPURA 0.00 \n28 UTTAR PRADESH 0.00 \n29 UTTARAKHAND 0.00 \n30 WEST BENGAL 124440.01 \n31 ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR 0.00 \n32 LAKSHADWEEP 0.00 \n33 PUDUCHERRY 33.37 \n34 THE DADRA AND NAGAR HAVELI \nAND DAMAN AND DIU 0.00 \n  Total 396331.40 \n (As per MIS) \n  \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure-II \n \nAnnexure-II referred in reply to part (a) & (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \nNo.401 due for answer on 30.11.2021 \n  \nState/UT wise details of pending liabilities for material component as on 25.11.2021 \nSl No. State/UT Material Liability (Rs. in Lakh) \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 134068.91 \n2 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 4519.9 \n3 ASSAM 6466.28 \n4 BIHAR 54832.56 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 26136.55 \n6 GOA 1.08 \n7 GUJARAT 11394.92 \n8 HARYANA 4594.65 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 4043.94 \n10 JAMMU AND KASHMIR 4019.34 \n11 JHARKHAND 20886.94 \n12 KARNATAKA 50854.94 \n13 KERALA 11737.22 \n14 LADAKH 35.5 \n15 MADHYA PRADESH 86182.33 \n16 MAHARASHTRA 8882.39 \n17 MANIPUR 6857.13 \n18 MEGHALAYA 11037.27 \n19 MIZORAM 24.98 \n20 NAGALAND 1099.75 \n21 ODISHA 76585.8 \n22 PUNJAB 15905.06 \n23 RAJASTHAN 83214.15 \n24 SIKKIM 877.85 \n25 TAMIL NADU 38998.24 \n26 TELANGANA 26007.55 \n27 TRIPURA 1593.8 \n28 UTTAR PRADESH 14879.43 \n29 UTTARAKHAND 12028.09 \n30 WEST BENGAL 107689.32 \n31 ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR 10 \n32 LAKSHADWEEP 0 \n33 PUDUCHERRY 8.33 \n34 THE DADRA AND NAGAR \nHAVELI AND DAMAN AND DIU 0 \n  Total 825474.2 \n(As per MIS) \n  \n \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure-III \n \n  \nAnnexure-III referred in reply to part (d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.401 due \nfor answer on for answer on 30.11.2021 \n  \nThe details of category wise completed and ongoing works along with expenditure under \nMahatma Gandhi NREGS in the State of Kerala in the FY 2021-22 (as on 26.11.2021) \nName of the category \nCompleted Ongoing \nNumber \nof works \nExpenditure  \n(Rs. in Lakh) \nNumber \nof works \nExpenditure \n(Rs. in \nLakh) \nRural Infrastructure 1184 834.48 4029 1449.21 \nBharat Nirman Sewa Kendra 0 0 9 7.02 \nCoastal Areas 0 0 0 0 \nDrought Proofing 3507 997.52 18067 8942.03 \nFisheries 8 0.1 25 0.55 \nFlood Control and Protection 3929 1793.03 9760 6800.93 \nFood Grain 0 0 0 0 \nLand Development 13541 4030.6 43382 31280.52 \nMicro Irrigation Works 3937 883.99 11842 5024.07 \nOther Works 0 0 101 2.38 \nPlay Ground 1 0 20 5.64 \nRenovation of traditional water bodies 1770 517.81 7355 1920.58 \nRural Connectivity 8560 16777.97 23038 26942.4 \nRural Drinking Water 76 3.19 686 1.44 \nRural Sanit