    "ls|LS17_S7_U_410": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 410 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30th NOVEMBER, 2021/AGRAHAYANA 9,1943 (SAKA) \n \nLOSSES DUE TO RAINS AND FLOODS \n \n410.  SHRI THIRUNAVUKKARASAR SU: \nSHRI SELVAM G.: \nSHRI M.K. RAGHAVAN: \nSHRI VIJAYAKUMAR (ALIAS) VIJAY VASANTH: \nSHRI C.N. ANNADURAI: \nSHRI GAJANAN KIRTIKAR: \nSHRIMATI NUSRAT JAHAN RUHI: \nSHRIMATI KANIMOZHI KARUNANIDHI: \nSHRI GAUTHAM SIGAMANI PON: \nSHRI VENKATESH NETHA BORLAKUNTA: \nSHRI PASUNOORI DAYAKAR: \nSHRI DHANUSH M. KUMAR: \nDR. G. RANJITH REDDY: \nDR. A. CHALLAKUMAR: \nSHRI PARTHIBAN S.R.: \nSHRIMATI KAVITHA MALOTHU: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether many States in the country have been  affected by heavy rains and \nconsequent flash floods, landslides, cloudbrusts, etc. in the recent months; \n \n(b) if so, whether any assessment has been made  by the Government about the \nnumber of persons killed,  displaced and missing along with loss of standing \ncrops, cattle and the extent of damage to property and monetary  loss, the details \nthereof, State/UT-wise including Telangana and Tamil Nadu and Kerala; \n \n(c) whether any Commission has been constituted  to study the loss and \nenvironmental damage caused due  to the incessant rain and floods and the \ndetails thereof; \n \n \n \n \n\n \n(d) the details of proposals received from the State  Governments to compensate \nthe said losses and  assistance sought, sanctioned and released by the Union  \nGovernment and through NDRF and SDRF along with  the criteria for it during the \nlast three years and the current year, year -wise and State/UT -wise including  \nTelangana, Tamil Nadu and Kerala; \n \n(e) the details of NDRF teams deployed in the affected States to take up damaged \nworks, help farmers,  etc., along with the number of persons rescued, State/UT -\nwise; and \n \n(f) the measures taken to evolve a permanent  mechanism to deal with such \ncalamities and thereby ensure safety of people and property in affected States? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n(a) to (d):  Various States in the country have been affected by natural calamities, \nincluding rains, flash flood, flood, landslides, cloudburst etc., during the monsoon \nseason of 2021. State -wise details of the losses of human lives, damage to \nproperty and loss of crops du e to hydro -meteorological calamities including \nfloods, landslides, during the year 2021 -22, as assessed/ reported by the State \nGovernments/ Union Territories including the States of Tamil Nadu and Kerala, \nare at Annexure -I.  No such details of losses have been reported by the State of \nTelangana, so far. \nThere are well established institutional mechanisms at the National and State \nlevel for the effective management of natural disasters. The primary \nresponsibility  of disaster  management, including   undertaking  disbursal   of  \nrelief   to  the   affected     people,  rests  with   the  State   Governments.    \n\n--2-- \nLS.US.Q.NO. 410 FOR 30.11.2021 \nFor providing relief to the affected people, in case of 12 notified natural disasters \nincluding flood, State Disaster Response Fund (SDRF) is already placed at the \ndisposal of the State Governments.  Additional financial assistance is provided \nfrom National Disaster Response Fund (NDRF), as per laid the down procedure in \ncase of disaster of ‘severe nature’, which includes an on the spot assessment of \ndamages by an Inter -Ministerial Central Team (IMCT) . The financial assistance is \ntowards relief and not for compensation of loss as suffered/ claimed.  The \nGuidelines on Constitution and Administration of National Disaster Response \nFund (NDRF) is available on website at https:// ndmindia.mha.gov. in/ \nimages/NDRFSDRF_06042017.pdf. No Commission has been constituted to study \nthe loss and environmental damage caused due to rain and flood by this Ministry. \nState-wise details of allocation and releases from SDRF/  State Disaster Risk \nManagement Fund (SDR MF) [after recommendations of 15 th Finance Commission, \nwhich includes SDRF and State Disaster Mitigation Fund (SDMF)] and NDRF during \nthe last three years and current year are given in Annexure-II. \n (e)    During the Monsoon season of 2021, National Disast er Response Force \n(NDRF) teams were deployed in the flood prone areas in the country and rescued/ \nevacuated stranded persons including farmers to safer places, as per details \ngiven in Annexure-III.  \n\n--3-- \nLS.US.Q.NO. 410 FOR 30.11.2021 \n(f)  There are institutional mechanisms at the National, State & district level in \nthe country to develop appropriate preparedness and prompt response \nmechanism for effective management of natural disasters. Central Government \nhas established a robust early warning system and has significantly enhanced the \naccuracy of weather forecasts.  Forecasting agencies are continuing their efforts \nfor the improvement of warning and dissemination systems vigorously. Mock \nexercises and community awareness programmes are being regularl y conducted \nto educate people/ farmers at the time of natural calamities. \nThe measures taken by the Central and State Governments have significantly \nimproved the disaster management practices, preparedness, prevention and \nresponse mechanism, resulting in s ignificant reduction in casualties during the \nnatural calamities in the country. Further, strengthening of the disaster \nmanagement is a continuing and evolving process of governance. \n***** \n  \n\n L.S.USQ NO. 410 FOR 30.11.2021 \n         Annexure-I \n \nState-wise details of damage due to cyclonic storms/ heavyrains/ floods/ landslides \netc. during 2021-22 \n   (Provisional) (As on 25.11.2021) \nSl. No. State Human \nLives lost (No.) \nCattle lost \n(No.) \nHouses/ huts \ndamaged \n(No.) \nCrops area \naffected  \n(in lakh ha.) \n1 2 3 4 5 6 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 40 2,875 4,026 1.51 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 6 18 98 0.02 \n3 Assam 26 1 390 0.67 \n4 Bihar 53 83 6,820 5.80 \n5 Chhattisgarh 16 279 1,986 -- \n6 Goa 3 16 3,402 0.001 \n7 Gujarat 162 9,922 1,32,710 1.49 \n8 Haryana 4 -- -- -- \n9 Himachal Pr. 298 1,235 1,186 0.07 \n10 Karnataka 144 1,705 57,526 13.98 \n11 Kerala 138 -- 9,720 0.85 \n12 Madhya Pr. 127 2,228 70,776 1.06 \n13 Maharashtra 489 4,400 53,653 4.55 \n14 Meghalaya 2 20 1,556 -- \n15 Nagaland 2 3,503 948 0.17 \n16 Odisha  19 4,632 28,929 1.82 \n17 Punjab 18 38 90 0.04 \n18 Rajasthan 51 1,556 37,368 6.79 \n19 Sikkim 9 51 1,098 0.02 \n20 Tamil Nadu 54 6,871 11,636 0.51 \n21 Tripura 6 33 1,796  \n22 Uttar Pradesh 162 277 11,335 3.61 \n23 Uttarakhand  107 523 1,057 0.54 \n24 West Bengal 65 12,958 3,40,748 6.90 \n25 UT of Daman & Diu 1 4 1,204 0.00 \n \nTotal 2,002 53,228 7,80,058 50.40 \n \n \n\nL.S.USQ NO. 410 FOR 30.11.2021 \nANNEXURE-II \n \nSTATEMENT SHOWING STATE-WISE DETAILS OF ALLOCATION AND RELEASE OF FUNDS UNDER SDRF/SDRMF AND NDRF DURING THE YEAR 2018-19 TO 2021-22 (AS \nON 25.11.2021) \n  (Rs. in crore) \nSl.No. State Allocation under SDRF/SDRMF including \nState share  \nCentre’s Share of SDRF/SDRMF Released Release from NDRF (For all calamities) \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \n1. Andhra Pradesh 509.00 534.00 1491.00 1192.80 458.10 324.15 1119.00 895.20 1004.88 570.91 657.029 -- \n2. Arunachal \nPradesh \n60.00 63.00 278.00 222.40 54.00 56.70 250.00 200.00 132.49 -- 59.34 -- \n3. Assam 532.00 559.00 858.00 686.40 478.80 503.10 772.00 617.60 -- -- 44.37 -- \n4. Bihar 543.00 570.00 1888.00 1510.40 101.815 631.12 1416.00 1132.80 -- 953.17 1255.27 -- \n5. Chhattisgarh 278.00 292.00 576.00 460.80 349.575 177.30 432.00 345.60 -- -- -- -- \n6. Goa 4.00 4.00 15.00 12.00 1.80 4.20 12.00 9.60 -- -- -- -- \n7. Gujarat 816.00 856.00 1765.00 1412.00 449.95 886.80 1324.00 1059.20 -- -- -- 1000.00 \n8. Haryana 356.00 