    "ls|LS17_S7_U_411": "GOVERNEM\nE\nNT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPART\nMENT OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 411\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30\nth\n \nNOVEMBER ,2021\n \n \nKISAN SAMMAN PENSION\n \n \n411\n.\n \nSHRI DINESH CHANDRA YADAV\n:\n \nSHRI MOHANBHAI\n \nKALYANJI KUNDARIYA:\n \nSHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR:\n \nSHRI DIPSINGH SHANKARSINH RATHOD:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare\nकृ \u0000षएवं\u0000कसानक\u0000याणमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased \nto state:\n \n(\na\n)\n \nwhether the farmers are categorized on the basis of their land holding as \nmarginal, small, medium and big by the Government, if so number of farmers in each \ncateg\nory, State\n-\nwise\n;\n \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nwhether the Government has formulated any pension scheme to improve quality \nof life of farmers especially small & marginal farmers (SMF), if so, the \nsalient features of \npension scheme for SMF;\n \n \n(\nc\n)\n \nthe number of farmers identified/enrolled for the said pension scheme district \nwise in Gujarat;\n \n \n(\nd\n)\n \nwhether the Kisan Samman Pension Yojana is applicable to all categories of the \nfarmers;\n \n \n(\ne\n)\n \nwhether the Government sc\nhemes for the welfare of the farmers are different for \nthe above categories farmers \nor all the schemes implemented are uniformly applicable to \nall farmers, if so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(\nf\n)\n \nwhether the Government is considering provision of Kisan Samman Pension\n \nto \nall eligible farmers who have been left out of Pradhan \nMantri\n \nKisan SammanNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) Yojana after a fresh survey; and \n \n \n(\ng\n)\n \nif so, the time by which the Government proposes to provide pension to such \nfarmers; and if not, the reasons therefor?\n \n \n\nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nकृ \u0000षएवं\u0000कसानक\u0000याणमं\u0000ी\n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a):\n \nYes,\n \nSir. The State\n-\nwise details of number of small, \nmarginal, medium and big \nlandholders\n \ncategorized on the basis of size of landholding has been placed at \nAnnexure\n-\nI.\n \n(b):\n \nPradhan Mantri Kisan MaanDhanYojna (PM\n-\nKMY), a Central Sector Scheme is \nbeing implemented in order to provide social security net for the Small and Marginal \nFarmers (SMF) \nby way of pension\n. \n \nUnder this scheme, a minimum fixed pension of Rs. \n3,000/\n-\n \nwill be provided to the eligible small and marginal farmers, subject to certain \nexclusion clauses, on attaining the age of 60 years.  The Scheme is a voluntary and \ncontributory p\nension scheme, with entry age of 18 to 40 years. The beneficiary can opt to \nbecome member of the Scheme by subscribing to a Pension Fund. The beneficiary \nwould be required to contribute Rs 100/ \n-\n \nper month at median entry age of 29 years. \nThe Central Gover\nnment shall also contribute to the Pension Fund in equal amount. \nContribution shall be made to a Pension Fund managed by the Life Insurance \nCorporation which will be responsible for pension pay out.\n \n \nUnder the scheme, farmers can also opt to allow his / her contribution to the \nScheme to be made from the benefits drawn from the Pradhan \nMantriKIsanSAmmanNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) Scheme directly.  The eligible farmers may, \ntherefore, enroll in the pension scheme t\nhrough the State Nodal Agencies under the \nPM\n-\nKISAN Scheme or through the Common Service Centres (CSCs) under Meity. \nExit \nfrom the scheme will be\n \nvoluntarily \nor on failure of contribution or on demise. On exit \nfrom the scheme, the beneficiary will receive h\nis/her accumulated share and the \nGovernment’s contribution will be deposited in the LIC Fund. After the subscriber’s \ndeath, the spouse or heir shall be entitled to receive 50% of the pension as family \npension, provided he/she is not already an SMF benefici\nary of the Scheme.  On the \ndeath of the subscriber during the period of contribution, the spouse shall have the \noption of continuing the Scheme by paying reg\nular contribution. There is\n \nan online \ngrievance redressal system for complete transparency. \n \n \n(c)\n \nT\nhe district\n-\nwise details of farmers enrolled under the Scheme in the State of \nGujarat is given at \nAnnexure\n-\nII.\n \n \n(d)\n \nUnder the Pradhan Mantri Kisan MaandhanYojana (PM\n-\nKMY), only the small and \nmarginal farmers having cultivable landholding upto 2 hectares\n \nan\nd in the age group of \n18\n-\n40 \nyears,\n \nsubject to certain exlusion criteria related with the higher income status, are \neligible to get enrolled. \n \n\n(e):\n \nThe eligibility criteria of the Government schemes for the welfare of the farmers \nvaries from one Scheme to a\nnother and every Schemes \nare implemented\n \nas per their \napproved Operational Guidelines. \n \n(f)\n& (g)\n:\n \n \nThe basic eligibility criteria for Pradhan Mantri Kisan SammanNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) and Pradhan Mantri Kisan MaandhanYojana\n \n(PM\n-\nKMY) is different. Under PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme, landholding, irrespective of its size, is the basic eligibility criteria to get \nthe benefit of the Scheme, while under PM\n-\nKMY only the small and marginal farmers in \nthe age group between 18\n-\n40 years, having th\ne cultivable landholding upto 2 hectares \nare eligible to get enrolled, subject to certain exclusion criteria related with higher income \nstatus. \n \n \nAs on 25.11.2021, more than 11.60 crore beneficiaries have been given the financial \nbenefits of the Scheme. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nState\n-\nwise estimated number of operational holdings as per Agriculture Census 2015\n-\n16\n \n(Number in ‘000)\n \nSl. \nNo.\n \nStates/UTs\n \nNumber of Operational Holdings\n \nMarginal \n(below 1.00 \nha.)\n \nSmall \n(1.00 \n-\n \n1.99 \nha.)\n \nSemi\n-\nmedium \n(2.00 \n-\n \n3.99 \nha.)\n \nMedium \n(4.00 \