    "ls|LS17_S7_U_433": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 433 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30th NOVEMBER, 2021/AGRAHAYANA 9,1943 (SAKA) \n \nNAXALS ENCOUNTER IN MAHARASHTRA \n \n433.  SHRIMATI VANGA GEETHA VISWANATH: \nSHRI KOTHA PRABHAKAR REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether Naxals were killed in an encounter in  Gadchiroli district, \nMaharashtra recently, if so, the details thereof during the last five years and the \ncurrent year, till date and the reasons therefor, State wise; \n \n(b) the number of naxals/police killed, injured in such encounters State-wise; \n \n(c) the number of fake encounters reported/along with the action taken thereon; \nand  \n \n(d) the corrective steps being taken by the  Government to stop such fake \nencounters? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n(a)& (b): 27 Left Wing Extremists (LWEs), including Milind  Teltumbde, Member, \nCentral Committee of CPI (Maoist), were killed in an exchange of fire (EoF)with \nPolice under the jurisdiction of Police Station Korchi, district Gadchiroli, \nMaharashtra on 13.11.2021. Following the EoF, the Police recovered 29 \nweapons, including AK -47 Rifle –06, Underbarrel Grenade Launcher –01, SLR \nRifle–09, INSAS Rifle–01, and .303 Rifle–03. \n \n\n--2-- \nLS.US.Q.NO. 433 FOR 30.11.2021 \nThe number of LWEs killed during the exchange of fire with security \nforces and security forces killed, injured during the last 05 years and the \ncurrent year, State-wise, is given at Annexure I. \n(c)& (d):No case  of fake encounter in the LWE affected States  has been \nreported. \nA strong constitutional and legal mechanism exists,  which include \nNational Human Rights Commission (NHRC) and State Human Rights \nCommission (SHRC), to prevent and deal with the case of fake encounter. NHRC \nhas issued guidelines for conducting magisterial enquiries in case of death of a \nperson in police action. The Hon’ble Supreme Court of India has also laid down  \na detailed procedure to be followed in investigation of a case of death of a \nperson during police encounter for thorough, effective and independent \ninvestigation. These mechanisms and rulings are in addition to the provisions \ngiven in the criminal laws for registration and fair investigation of an offence. \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nLSUQ No. 433 for 30.11.2021 \nSecurity Forces martyred/injured and LWEs killed from 2016 to 15.11.2021 \n    Security Forces martyred \nS.No. State 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 \n(Upto15.11.2021) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n2 Bihar 11 0 1 1 0 0 \n3 Chhattisgarh 11 16 10 4 22 24 \n4 Jharkhand 2 2 3 2 1 1 \n5 Madhya Pradesh 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n6 Maharashtra 0 1 0 0 2 0 \n7 Odisha 1 0 0 1 2 0 \n8 Telangana 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n9 West Bengal 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n10 Kerala 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n  Total 25 19 14 8 27 25 \n \n    LWEs Killed \nS.No. State 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 \n(Upto15.11.2021 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 3 2 0 7 0 6 \n2 Bihar 12 7 2 7 5 6 \n3 Chhattisgarh 135 75 125 78 42 37 \n4 Jharkhand 20 12 26 26 13 5 \n5 Madhya Pradesh 0 0 0 2 3 3 \n6 Maharashtra 9 17 52 8 9 49 \n7 Odisha 40 8 19 8 17 6 \n8 Telangana 0 9 1 2 10 1 \n9 West Bengal 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n10 Kerala 2 0 0 5 1 0 \n  Total 221 130 225 143 100 113 \n \n  \n\nLSUQ No. 433 for 30.11.2021 \n \n  \n  Security Forces injured \nS.No. State 2016 2017 2018 2019 2020 2021 \n(Upto15.11.2021 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 1 0 1 1 1 0 \n2 Bihar 8 0 4 1 2 0 \n3 Chhattisgarh 98 78 117 36 85 72 \n4 Jharkhand 16 14 11 25 6 8 \n5 Madhya Pradesh 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n6 Maharashtra 21 40 15 15 9 10 \n7 Odisha 1 21 3 4 4 3 \n8 Telangana 0 0 1 0 1 0 \n9 West Bengal 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n10 Kerala 0 0 0 0 0 0 \n  Total 145 153 152 82 108 93 \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_435": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 435 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nJOB CARD HOLDERS UNDER MGNREGS \n \n435.  SHRI MANNE SRINIVAS REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has any details of the job card holders under the MGNREGS \nand wages fixed to them, State/UT-wise and gender-wise; \n(b)  whether it is a fact that many workers are being paid less/not being paid fully in some \nStates; \n(c)  if so, the details of such cases reported so far and the action taken so far; and \n(d)  the details of the funds released under this scheme during each of the last three years \nand the current year, State/UT-wise along with the steps being taken to pay the wages \nto card holders timely? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a) to (c):    The Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (Mahatma \nGandhi NREGA), 2005, is an Act to provide f or the enhancement of livelihood security of \nthe household in rural areas of the country by providing at least one hundred days of \nguaranteed wage employment in a financial year to every household whose adult members \nvolunteer to do unskilled manual work. States/UTs-wise number of households having Job \ncards is given at Annexure-I.  \n  \nAs per section 6(1) of Mahatma Gandhi NREGA 2005 (Mahatma Gandhi NREGA), the \nCentral Government may, by notification, specify the wage rate for unskilled work for its \nbeneficiaries. Accordingly, the Ministry of Rural Development notifies Mahatma Gandhi \nNREGA wage rate every year for States/UTs. The wage rate is made applicable from  1st \nApril of each financial year.   The State/UT wise wage rates for unskilled workers und er \nMahatma Gandhi NREGA for the Financial Year 2021-22, are at Annexure-II. \n  \nAs per the Para 17 of Schedule -I of the Act, “The State Government shall link the \nwages, without any gender bias, with the quantity of work done and it shall be paid according \nto the rural schedule of rates fixed after time and motion studies for different types of work \nand different seasons and revised periodically”. This is being inbuilt into the design of the \nscheme and being scrupulously observed. \n  \n(d):      State/UT-wise details of Central fund released under Mahatma Gandhi NREGA in last \nthree financial years and current financial year 2021 -22 (as on 25.11.2021) is given at \nAnnexure-III. \n  \n \n\n \nDirect wage payments to the accounts of beneficiaries are being made through National  \nElectronic Fund management System (NeFMS) using DBT protocol. To monitor the progress \nof payment made to wage seekers, a payment dashboard has been development. Also regular \nreview with Stakeholders (Banks, PFMS, and States) is taking place. \nFurther, in o rder to monitor the timely payment of wages, this Ministry reviews the \nprogress of States, via Labour Budget Meeting, Labour Budget Revision Meeting, Mid -Term \nReview Meeting and other interactions with the States/UTs.  \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure I \n  \nAnnexure-I referred in reply to parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \nNo.435 dated 30.11.2021 \n(Figure in lakh) \nSl. No. States/UTs \nNumber of households having Job \ncards under Mahatma Gandhi \nNREGA (as on 26.11.2021) \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 97.81 \n2 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 2.77 \n3 ASSAM 54.89 \n4 BIHAR 189.32 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 40.59 \n6 GOA 0.34 \n7 GUJARAT 42.64 \n8 HARYANA 12.00 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 13.86 \n10 JAMMU AND KASHMIR 12.40 \n11 JHARKHAND 59.64 \n12 KARNATAKA 75.25 \n13 KERALA 40.07 \n14 LADAKH 0.37 \n15 MADHYA PRADESH 77.42 \n16 MAHARASHTRA 94.01 \n17 MANIPUR 5.90 \n18 MEGHALAYA 6.24 \n19 MIZORAM 2.09 \n20 NAGALAND 4.49 \n21 ODISH