    "ls|LS17_S7_U_439": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 439 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nRURAL DEVELOPMENT WORK UNDER CORPORATE SOCIAL \nRESPONSIBILITY \n \n439.  SHRI HEMANT TUKARAM GODSE: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether many new initiatives have been taken  for the inclusive development in rural \nareas of the country under Corporate Social Responsibility during  the last three years, \nif so, the details thereof; \n(b)  the details of expenditure incurred and work  executed on rural development under \nCorporate Social Responsibility during each of the last three years; and \n(c)  whether any study on appraisal of work under  Corporate Social Responsibility has \nbeen undertaken? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a) & (b) : As per the information shared by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs(MoCA), the \nGovernment provides a broad framework for Corporate Social Responsibility(CSR) through \nSection 135 of the Companies Act, 2013 (‘Act’), Schedule VII of the Act and Companies \n(CSR Policy) Rules, 2014. Schedule VII of the Act indicates the activities that can be \nundertaken by the company as eligible CSR activities. Further, MoCA clarified that items \nmentioned in Schedule VII are broad based and must be interpreted liberally to captur e the \nessence of the subject enumerated. Item no. (x) Schedule VII of Companies Act, 2013 \nmentions \"Rural Development Projects\" as eligible CSR activities. On the basis of filing \nmade by companies in the MoCA registry, CSR funds spent by various companies in \"Rural \nDevelopment Projects\" under the Act for the financial years 2017 -18, 2018-19 and 2019 -20 \nare given below:  \n \nS.No FY Expenditure incurred for the Rural Development projects (In Crores) \n1 2017-18 1,724.07 \n2 2018-19  2,428.45 \n3 2019-20 2,279.20 \n*Source: National CSR Data Portal. All data related to CSR (State/UT -wise as well as \ndevelopment sector wise) as filed by companies in MoCA 21 registry is available in public \ndomain at www.csr.gov.in.The expenditure details for FY 2020-21 are not yet available with \nMoCA. \n\n \nFurther, the Ministry of Rural Development has leveraged the funds under CSR for the \nconvergence-based schemes such as Saansad Adarsh Gram Yojana(SAGY) and Shyama \nPrasad Mukherji Rurban Mission (SPMRM) for converging private / corporate investments \nwith the government initiatives for the development of Gram Panchayats/clusters identified \nunder these schemes. The details of expenditure incurred in the clusters of Shyama Prasad \nMukherji Rurban Miss ion (SPMRM) is placed in the annexure.However, the expenditure \nincurred under CSR in SAGY is not maintained centrally by this Ministry. \n \n(c) :  The Ministry of Corporate Affairs and the Ministry of Rural Development have not \nundertaken any specific study on appraisal of work under Corporate Social Responsibility. \n \n******* \n\n1 \nAnnexure-I \n \nAnnexure-I referred in point (a) and (b) of reply to Lok Sabha unstarred question No. 439 scheduled for answer on 30th November 2021 \n \nList of the works wherein CSR funds are involved in the Clusters identified under Shyama Prasad Mukherji Rurban Mission (SPMRM)  \n \n \nList of the works wherein CSR  funds are involved \n(All financial figures in rupees) \nWork type both means that the funds from CGF have also been utilised partly \nS.N\no \nState  District  Cluster  Work Name Component \nName \nWork Type CGF \nAllocati\non  \nConvergenc\ne \nAllocation \nTotal \nAllocation \nCGF  \nExpen\nditure \nConvergenc\ne \nExpenditur\ne \nTotal \nExpendi\nture \n1 Chhattis\ngarh                                       \n                                     \nBastar Madpal Primary Shala Madpal \nMiddle  Shala Gidodwar \nAnganwadi Gidodwar  \nFurniture  Jhula Water \nCooler \