    "ls|LS17_S7_U_450": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \n \nUN\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n450\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n30\nth\n \nNOVEMBER\n, 2021\n \n \nCOLLABORATION FOR DIGITAL TRANSACTIONS UNDER ENAM\n \n \n450\n. \n \nDR. S\nUKANTA MAJUMDAR:\n \nSHRI VINOD KUMAR SONKAR:\n \nSHRIMATI SANGEETA KUMARI SINGH\n \nDEO:\n \nSHRI RAJA AMARESHWARA NAIK:\n \nSHRI BHOLA SINGH:\n \nDR. JAYANTA KUMAR ROY:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS\n \nWELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has collaborated with a\n \nprivate bank for National \nAgriculture Market (eNAM) to\n \nenable digital collections and settlement of \nfunds to\n \nvarious eNAM beneficiaries in the country, \nif so, the\n \ndetails thereof;\n \n(b)\n \nthe number of registered farmers and traders on\n \neNAM and who have \nbenefitted from the digital\n \nmarketplace;\n \n(c) \n \nthe total value of agri\n-\nproduce traded on eNAM\n \nso far since its inception;\n \n(d) \n \nthe achievements made by the Sma\nll Farmers\n \nAgri\n-\nBusiness Consortium \n(SFAC) set up as the nodal\n \nimplementing agency by the Ministry since its \ninception;\n \n(e) \n \nwhether the SFAC is implementing Central\n \nSector Scheme (CSS) on \n“Formation & Promotion of\n \n10000 FPOs” across the country, if so, th\ne details \nthereof;\n \nand\n \n(f) \n \nthe other steps being taken by the Government\n \nfor development of agriculture \nand welfare of farmers in\n \nBolangir constituency of Odisha?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS\n \nWELFARE\n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI NA\nRENDRA SINGH\n \nTOMAR)\n \n(a)\n:\n \n \nSmall Farmers Agribusiness Consortium(SFAC) under aegis of Ministry of \nAgriculture & Farmers Welfare, Government of India has empanelled banks viz. Axis \nBank Limited, Kotak Mahindra Bank Limited, HDFC Bank, Indusind Bank Limited &\n \nICICI Bank for provisioning of payment & settlement services for National Agriculture \n\nMarket (eNAM) transactions. The empanelment of above mentioned banks enable \ncollections and settlement of funds to various eNAM registered beneficiaries across \nthe count\nry. \n \n(b)\n:\n \n \nAs on 31\nst\n \nOctober 2021, a total of 1.7 crore farmers and 1.98 lakh traders \nhave registered themselves and many of them have benefitted from National \nAgriculture Market(e\n-\nNAM). \n \n \n(c)\n:\n \n \nAs on 31\nst\n \nOctober, 2021, the total value of Agri\n-\nproduce tr\naded on e\n-\nNAM is \nworth Rs. Rs. 1,50,664 Crore.\n \n \n(d) & (e)\n:\n \n \nSFAC is one of the Implementing Agencies under the Central Sector \nScheme for formation and promotion of \n10,000 \nFPOs.\n \nUnder the Scheme, SFAC has \nbeen allotted target for formation and promotion of \n566 FPOs during 2020\n-\n21, out of \nwhich 442 FPOs have been registered so far.\n \n \n \n       \nFurther, SFAC is\n \nalso\n \nimplementing schemes of Venture Capital \nAssistance(VCA) and National Agriculture Market (e\n-\nNAM).\n \n \n \n(f)\n:\n \n \nAs informed by Govt. of Odisha, the major sc\nhemes are implemented in the \nBolangir District  of Odisha as at Annexure\n-\nI.\n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \nThe following major schemes are being implemented in the district for the \ndevelopment of agriculture and welfare of farmers\n \nState Plan Scheme\n \ni\n.\n \nInput subsidy \n \nii\n.\n \nPromotion o\nf improved Agronomic Package of Practices\n \niii\n.\n \nPromotion of Integrated farming\n \niv\n.\n \nManagement of Soil Health \n \nv\n.\n \nPromotion of Need based Plant Protection \n \nvi\n.\n \nSubsidy under Agriculture Policy \n \nvii\n.\n \nPopularisation of Agriculture Implements & Equipments \n \nviii\n.\n \nKrushak Assistance for L\nivelihood and Income Augmentation\n(\nKALIA\n)\n \nix\n.\n \nSpecial programme for Millets in Tribal Areas.\n \n \nCentral Sector plan Scheme\n \n \ni\n.\n \nNational Food Security Mission (NFSM) Pulses, Oilseeds & Commercial \nCrops\n \nii\n.\n \nBringing Green Revolution to Eastern India\n \n(BGREI)\n \niii\n.\n \nVariety development for pulses under ICARDA\n \niv\n.\n \ne\n-\npest surveillance & pest management\n \nv\n.\n \nPradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana\n \nvi\n.\n \nPM\n-\nKISAN\n \nvii\n.\n \nNational Agriculture Market(e\n-\nNAM)\n \nviii\n.\n \nEstablishment of Mini\n-\nsoil testing lab at all blocks\n \n*****\n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_451": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 451 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nINCENTIVE UNDER PMGSY \n \n451.  SHRI PINAKI MISRA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of roads constructed under the  Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana \n(PMGSY) during each of the last three years, State/UT-wise, including in Odisha; \n(b)  the criteria for setting road construction targets; \n(c)  the details of financial incentives given to best  performing States, particularly with \nregard to maintenance of roads; \n(d)  the criteria for determining the best performing States; and \n(e)  the status of implementation of the Electronic  Maintenance of PMGSY roads \n(eMARG) initiative, and the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a)  The details of roads constructed under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) \nduring the last three years and current year, State/ UT -wise, including in Odisha are given at \nAnnexure-I. \n(b)  The criteria for road construction targets are set annually in consultation with the States, \nkeeping in view the balance works left with the States, capacity of the State Executing \nAgencies and anticipated sanction of projects during the year. \n  \n(c) to (d) Maintenance of roads constructed under the programme is the responsibility of the \nState Governments and all road works are covered by initial five year maintenance contract to \nbe entered into along with the construction contract, with the same contractor , as per the \nStandard Bidding Document. Maintenance funds are to be provided by the State Government. \nMaintenance of roads beyond 5 years is also to be done by the State Government.  \n  \nSince 2016 -17, financial incentives are being given to top performing States, which show \nhigher achievement in the year on the basis of set parameters. These funds are to be used by \nthe States for renewal of roads after 5 year Defect Liability Period (DLP) . The current \nparameters for determining the best performing States for grant of financial incentives under \nPMGSY, which are applicable since 2020-21 are as under:-  \n(i) Achievement of Target Length during the year. \n(ii) Achievement of Target Habitations during the year. \n(iii) Length constructed using New Technology during the year. \n(iv) Expenditure on maintenance of roads within Defect Liability Period (DLP) \n(v) Road Length renewed during the year post DLP. \n(vi) Quality of maintenance works as brought out by National Quality Monitor \nInspections. \n\n \nThe details of financial incentive released to States during the last 4 financial years and \nthe current year are given at Annexure-II. \n(e)    As a measure of enhancing the focus on  maintenance of roads during the defect liability \nperiod (five years from the date of completion of road) and streamlining the delivery of \nroutine maintenance of PMGSY roads on the basis of performance based maintenance \ncontract, eMARG has been implemented in all the states. eMARG is an online platform, used \nby all the states, that monitors maintenance of PMGSY works for five years since the date of \ncompletion (i.e. under Defect Liability Period -DLP) \neMARG is currently getting utilized across 27 states and 2 UTs by 1,254 (97%) PIUs. 11,466 \n(89%) contractors have been onboarded on eMARG. Out of 42957 roads under DLP, 93% \nhave been registered on eMARG. Since FY 2019 -20, payment of 4,27,810 bills amounting to \na total of Rs. 970 crore  has been made to contractors through eMARG. Out of which, Rs. \n444.00 crore has been paid during FY 2021-22. \n  \n***** \n  \n\n            Annexure-I \n  \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No 451 due \nfor reply on 30.11.2021 \nDetails of roads (Km) constructed under PMGSY during the last three years and \ncurrent year \nSr.No. State/UT 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 (upto \n25.11.2021) \n1 Andaman And \nNicobar Islands (UT) \n \n0 0 31 10 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 337 301 531 592 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 1318 1731 1796 106 \n4 Assam 4295 3647 2682 641 \n5 Bihar 4222 719 2255 853 \n6 Chhattisgarh 3112 1952 4688 803 \n7 Goa 0 0 0 0 \n8 Gujarat 14 0 202 80 \n9 Haryana 5 0 224 1013 \n10 Himachal Pradesh 1334 1087 1916 1297 \n11 Jammu And Kashmir 1559 1175 3167 1414 \n12 Jharkhand 3570 1408 2008 367 \n13 Karnataka 6 6 566 1028 \n14 Kerala 314 126 77 17 \n15 Madhya Pradesh 4521 1872 2956 1929 \n16 Maharashtra 267 120 181 27 \n17 Manipur 852 754 893 108 \n18 Meghalaya 211 274 728 340 \n19 Mizoram 267 345 246 187 \n20 Nagaland 209 189 36 62 \n21 Odisha 8130 5298 1844 290 \n22 Pondicherry (UT) 0 0 0 0 \n23 Punjab 247 29 1 69 \n24 Rajasthan 2528 103 1856 1803 \n25 Sikkim 352 68 157 44 \n26 Tamilnadu 2167 1066 871 975 \n27 Tripura 169 85 109 72 \n28 Uttar Pradesh 1688 376 711 345 \n29 Uttarakhand 1756 2036 3365 501 \n30 West Bengal 5111 2180 2179 180 \n31 Telangana 381 206 315 313 \n32 Ladakh (UT) 63 151 86 109 \nTotal 49,007 27,305 36674 15573 \n  \n  \n\n Annexure-II \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (b) to (d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No \n451 due for reply on 30.11.2021 \n  \nFinancial Incentive Details[Rs in Crore] \nS.No State/UT 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \n1 Andhra Pradesh - 52.37 32.98 39.60 36.47 \n2 Assam 73.76 - 36.18 - - \n3 Bihar 74.77 - 79.43 - - \n4 Chhattisgarh - - - 75.15 87.44 \n5 Haryana 20.25 - 13.2 15.67 - \n6 Himachal Pradesh 86.61 39.39 26.12 32.59 - \n7 Jammu & Kashmir - - 9.31 - - \n8 Jharkhand - 34.37 - - - \n9 Karnataka 71.95 - 46.63 - 47.12 \n10 Kerala - - 5.11 6.66 - \n11 Madhya Pradesh 200.24 219.55 144.19 180.27 198.18 \n12 Manipur 15.82 12.5 - - - \n13 Meghalaya 5.9 4.36 - - - \n14 Odisha 175.67 109.61 73.68 95.94 155.48 \n15 Punjab 20.66 20.42 - - - \n16 Rajasthan - 230.36 150.05 184.74 - \n17 Sikkim