    "ls|LS17_S7_U_452": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 452 \n  ANSWERED ON 30/11/2021 \n \nGROWTH IN RURAL WAGES \n \n452.  SHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the growth in rural wages, after adjusting for  inflation since January, 2014, month -\nwise; \n(b)  whether the Government is of the opinion that  current rural wage rates are adequate \nenough to maintain a rural household; \n(c)  if so, the reasons thereto; and \n(d)  if not, the measures being taken by the Government to increase rural wages? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a):       As per the information shared by Labour Bureau, Ministry of Labour & Employment, \nLabour Bureau compiles and maintains average daily wage rate data in respect of selected \nagricultural and non -agricultural occupations on the basis of the data coll ected by the Field \nOperation Division (FOD) of National Statistical Office (NSO), Ministry of Statistics & \nProgramme Implementation from a fixed set of 600 sample villages spread over 20 States.  \n \n     Month-wise average daily wage rate  in respect of Non Agricultural Occupation along \nwith Consumer Price Index for Rural Labourer (CPI -RL) from January 2014 to September, \n2021 is given at Annexure-I. \n  \n(b) to (d):          As per section 6(1) of Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment \nGuarantee Act, 2005 (Maha tma Gandhi NREGA), the Central Government may, by \nnotification, specify the wage rate for unskilled work for its beneficiaries.  Accordingly, the \nMinistry of Rural Development notifies wage rate  under Mahatma Gandhi NREGA every \nfinancial year for States/UT s. To compensate the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural \nEmployment Guarantee Scheme (Mahatma Gandhi NREGS) workers against inflation, the \nMinistry of Rural Development revises the wage rates every financial year based on \nConsumer Price Index for Agricultural Labourer (CPI-AL). The wage rate is made applicable \nfrom 1st April of each financial year. \n   \nState/UT-wise notified wage rates for unskilled worker under Mahatma Gandhi NREGA for \nthe financial years from 2014-15 to 2021-22 is given at Annexure-II. \n  \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-I referred in reply to part (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 452 \ndated 30.11.2021 \n  \nMonth-wise average daily notified wage rates  in respect of Non Agricultural Occupation \nalong with Consumer Price Index for Rural Labourer (CPI -RL) from Jan uary 2014 to \nSeptember, 2021 \n  \nYear Month Wage Rate CPI-RL Year Month \nWage \nRate CPI-RL \n2014 \nJanuary 234.08 759 \n2018 \nJanuary 277.31 901 \nFebruary 234.39 759 February 278.03 896 \nMarch 232.69 765 March 278.94 894 \nApril 233.21 773 April 279.20 896 \nMay 232.41 780 May 279.82 899 \nJune 233.63 787 June 280.92 902 \nJuly 234.45 801 July 282.05 910 \nAugust 236.28 810 August 284.49 915 \nSeptember 237.20 813 September 285.20 917 \nOctober 238.69 815 October 285.24 920 \nNovember 238.36 816 November 286.00 921 \nDecember 240.70 810 December 287.27 921 \n2015 \nJanuary 241.32 808 \n2019 \nJanuary 288.71 923 \nFebruary 242.77 806 February 288.95 925 \nMarch 243.46 807 March 289.43 932 \nApril 243.78 809 April 289.96 939 \nMay 245.33 816 May 291.20 948 \nJune 245.65 824 June 291.82 957 \nJuly 248.27 827 July 292.08 965 \nAugust 249.57 836 August 293.22 972 \nSeptember 250.65 843 September 293.29 983 \nOctober 249.26 853 October 294.09 993 \nNovember 250.19 857 November 294.62 1006 \nDecember 251.63 857 December 295.03 1019 \n2016 \nJanuary 253.79 854 \n2020 \nJanuary 296.63 1021 \nFebruary 253.52 849 February 297.29 1016 \nMarch 254.53 848 March 297.25 1013 \nApril 254.75 854 *April  - 1019 \nMay 254.79 866 May 319.47 1025 \nJune 255.70 874 June 319.23 1024 \nJuly 256.78 881 July 320.99 1028 \nAugust 258.33 881 August 316.04 1033 \nSeptember 261.89 877 September 310.88 1043 \nOctober 263.15 881 October 311.37 1057 \nNovember 263.70 883 November 311.01 1065 \nDecember 264.50 881 December 311.92 1053 \n2017 \nJanuary 266.38 876 \n2021 \nJanuary 313.69 1045 \nFebruary 267.67 874 February 316.00 1044 \nMarch 268.23 872 March 317.62 1043 \nApril 268.89 876 April 318.43 1049 \nMay 269.05 878 May 320.18 1057 \nJune 270.03 884 June 320.22 1065 \nJuly 271.04 890 July 322.60 1070 \n\nAugust 272.61 900 August 323.35 1074 \nSeptember 273.73 899 September 325.58 1076 \nOctober 274.85 907 Average daily wage rate has been compiled \nand released up to September, 2021. November 275.86 910 \nDecember 275.72 906 \n*Due to Covid pandemic, the data for the month of April, 2020 could not be collected and \ncomplied.  \n  \n  \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-II referred in reply to part (b) to (d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \nNo.452 dated 30.11.2021 \n  \nState/UT-wise notified wage rates for unskilled worker under Mahatma Gandhi \nNREGA for the financial years from 2014-15 to 2021-22. \n (In Rs.) \nSl. \nNo. States \nFY \n2014-15 \nFY \n2015-16 \nFY \n2016-17 \nFY \n2017-18 \nFY \n2018-19 \nFY \n2019-20 \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH   169 180 194 197 205 211 \n2 ARUNACHAL \nPRADESH   155 167 172 177 177 192 \n3 ASSAM   167 179 182 183 189 193 \n4 BIHAR   158 162 167 168 168 171 \n5 CHHATTISGARH   157 159 167 172 174 176 \n6 GOA 195 208 229 240 254 254 \n7 GUJARAT   167 178 188 192 194 199 \n8 HARYANA   236 251 259 277 281 284 \n9 HIMACHAL \nPRADESH \nNon-\nscheduled \nAreas-154 \nScheduled \nAreas-193 \nNon-\nscheduled \nAreas-162 \nScheduled \nAreas-203 \nNon-\nscheduled \nAreas-170 \nScheduled \nAreas-213 \nNon-\nscheduled \nAreas-179 \nScheduled \nAreas- \n224 \nNon-scheduled \nAreas-184 \nScheduled Areas-\n230 \nNon-\nscheduled \nAreas-185 \nScheduled \nAreas-231 \n10 JAMMU AND \nKASHMIR   157 164 173 179 186 189 \n11 JHARKHAND   158 162 167 168 168 171 \n12 KARNATAKA 191 204 224 236 249 249 \n13 KERALA   212 229 240 258 271 271